window.COURSE_DATA={"parts":[{"id":"p1","order":1,"title":{"id":"Fondasi PAM dan Mental Model","en":"PAM Foundations and Mental Models"},"desc":{"id":"Mengerti mengapa PAM ada dan memisahkan session flow dari credential flow.","en":"Understand why PAM exists and separate session flow from credential flow."}},{"id":"p2","order":2,"title":{"id":"Arsitektur dan Administrasi","en":"Architecture and Administration"},"desc":{"id":"Vault, PVWA, CPM, PSM, Safe, Platform, permission, dan account lifecycle.","en":"Vault, PVWA, CPM, PSM, Safes, Platforms, permissions, and account lifecycle."}},{"id":"p3","order":3,"title":{"id":"Troubleshooting L2","en":"L2 Troubleshooting"},"desc":{"id":"Log, timeline, SAML, PSM, AppLocker, dan evidence-based isolation.","en":"Logs, timelines, SAML, PSM, AppLocker, and evidence-based isolation."}},{"id":"p4","order":4,"title":{"id":"Implementasi dan Deployment","en":"Implementation and Deployment"},"desc":{"id":"Discovery, design, build, pilot, rollout, Self-Hosted, dan Privilege Cloud.","en":"Discovery, design, build, pilot, rollout, Self-Hosted, and Privilege Cloud."}},{"id":"p5","order":5,"title":{"id":"Reliability dan Integrasi","en":"Reliability and Integrations"},"desc":{"id":"HA/DR, backup, recovery, API, SIEM, ITSM, serta identity integration.","en":"HA/DR, backup, recovery, APIs, SIEM, ITSM, and identity integrations."}},{"id":"p6","order":6,"title":{"id":"L2 Mastery dan Onboarding","en":"L2 Mastery and Onboarding"},"desc":{"id":"Ticket ownership, RCA, escalation, learning from ticket history, dan roadmap 90 hari.","en":"Ticket ownership, RCA, escalation, ticket-history learning, and a 90-day roadmap."}}],"modules":{"m1":{"id":"m1","title":"Mengapa PAM Dibutuhkan","en":"Why PAM Exists","phase":"1. Dasar Sistem","phaseEn":"1. Core Mechanics","lead":"Memahami risiko akun privileged dan alasan kontrol biasa belum cukup.","leadEn":"Understand privileged-account risk and why ordinary controls are not enough.","objId":["Membedakan akun biasa dan akun privileged","Menjelaskan masalah yang diselesaikan CyberArk","Mengenali kontrol preventif, detektif, dan audit"],"objEn":["Differentiate standard and privileged accounts","Explain the problems CyberArk solves","Recognize preventive, detective, and audit controls"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Mulai dari risikonya, bukan produknya</h2><p>Akun privileged seperti Domain Admin, root, local administrator, database administrator, dan service account dapat mengubah konfigurasi, membaca data sensitif, mematikan kontrol keamanan, atau menghapus jejak. Karena dampaknya besar, password yang kuat saja belum cukup. Organisasi juga perlu mengontrol siapa yang boleh memakai akun, kapan akses diberikan, dari jalur mana koneksi dibuat, dan apa yang dilakukan selama sesi.</p><h3>Masalah yang biasanya muncul tanpa PAM</h3><ul><li>Password dibagikan lewat chat atau spreadsheet.</li><li>Satu account dipakai banyak orang sehingga audit tidak dapat menunjuk pelaku sebenarnya.</li><li>Password service account tidak pernah diganti karena tim takut aplikasi berhenti.</li><li>User membuka koneksi langsung dari laptop ke production sehingga malware atau clipboard berisiko ikut masuk.</li></ul><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Mental model:</strong> CyberArk bukan hanya tempat menyimpan password. PAM menggabungkan vaulting, authorization, credential rotation, session isolation, recording, dan audit.</div><h3>Cara berpikir L2</h3><p>Ketika ada ticket, jangan mulai dari “komponen mana yang harus direstart”. Mulai dari aktivitas yang gagal: login ke portal, melihat account, mengambil password, memulai session, atau merotasi credential. Aktivitas tersebut menentukan flow dan evidence yang perlu diperiksa.</p></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Start with the risk, not the product</h2><p>Privileged identities such as Domain Admin, root, local administrator, database administrator, and service accounts can change configuration, read sensitive data, disable security controls, or remove evidence. A strong password is not enough. The organization must also control who may use an account, when access is allowed, which path the connection follows, and what happens during the session.</p><h3>Typical failures without PAM</h3><ul><li>Passwords are shared through chat or spreadsheets.</li><li>One account is used by many people, so the audit trail cannot identify the real operator.</li><li>Service-account passwords are never changed because teams fear an outage.</li><li>Users connect directly from endpoints to production, exposing credentials and sessions to endpoint threats.</li></ul><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Mental model:</strong> CyberArk is not only a password store. PAM combines vaulting, authorization, credential rotation, session isolation, recording, and audit.</div><h3>The L2 viewpoint</h3><p>Do not begin a ticket by asking which service to restart. First identify the failed activity: portal authentication, account listing, password retrieval, session launch, or credential rotation. That activity tells you which flow and evidence set matter.</p></div>","part":"p1","order":1,"duration":18,"level":"foundation","tags":["PAM","risk","audit"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Klasifikasi risiko privileged","en":"Classify privileged risk"},"brief":{"id":"Ambil lima account dari environment contoh. Jelaskan dampak jika credential bocor, kontrol yang dibutuhkan, dan evidence audit yang diharapkan.","en":"Take five accounts from a sample environment. Explain the impact of credential exposure, required controls, and expected audit evidence."},"deliverables":{"id":["Tabel account, owner, privilege, impact, control.","Satu paragraf perbedaan IAM biasa dan PAM.","Daftar tiga risiko shared credential."],"en":["Account, owner, privilege, impact, and control table.","One paragraph explaining IAM versus PAM.","Three shared-credential risks."]},"safety":{"id":"Gunakan data dummy; jangan memasukkan identifier atau credential customer.","en":"Use dummy data; never enter customer identifiers or credentials."}}},"m2":{"id":"m2","title":"Dua Flow Utama: Session dan Credential","en":"The Two Flows: Session and Credential","phase":"1. Dasar Sistem","phaseEn":"1. Core Mechanics","lead":"Membedakan jalur PSM dan CPM agar troubleshooting tidak salah arah.","leadEn":"Separate the PSM and CPM paths so troubleshooting starts in the right place.","objId":["Menggambar session flow","Menggambar credential flow","Memilih komponen berdasarkan gejala"],"objEn":["Draw the session flow","Draw the credential flow","Choose a component from the symptom"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Satu ticket, dua jalur yang berbeda</h2><p>PSM mengatur jalur akses user menuju target. CPM mengatur lifecycle password. Keduanya dapat memakai account yang sama, tetapi kegagalannya menghasilkan gejala dan log yang berbeda.</p><div class=\"diagram\"><b>SESSION FLOW</b>\nUser → PVWA → PSM/PSMP → Target\nTujuan: koneksi terisolasi, direkam, dan diaudit.\n\n<b>CREDENTIAL FLOW</b>\nCPM → Vault → Target → Change/Verify → Vault\nTujuan: password target dan password di Vault tetap sinkron.</div><h3>Contoh isolasi cepat</h3><ul><li>Tombol Connect tidak terlihat: mulai dari permission Safe, platform/connection component, dan entitlement.</li><li>Tombol ada tetapi session putus: mulai dari PSM, dispatcher, AppLocker, network PSM-to-target, dan target.</li><li>Connect gagal karena password salah setelah rotasi: telusuri CPM, Verify/Change/Reconcile, dan dependency.</li></ul><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Kesalahan umum:</strong> Merestart CPM untuk masalah session. CPM tidak membangun layar RDP atau SSH user.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>One ticket can involve two different paths</h2><p>PSM controls the user-access path to a target. CPM controls the password lifecycle. They may use the same account, but failures produce different symptoms and logs.</p><div class=\"diagram\"><b>SESSION FLOW</b>\nUser → PVWA → PSM/PSMP → Target\nPurpose: isolate, record, and audit the connection.\n\n<b>CREDENTIAL FLOW</b>\nCPM → Vault → Target → Change/Verify → Vault\nPurpose: keep the target password synchronized with the Vault.</div><h3>Quick isolation examples</h3><ul><li>Connect is missing: start with Safe permissions, platform or connection-component mapping, and entitlement.</li><li>Connect exists but the session drops: start with PSM, the dispatcher, AppLocker, PSM-to-target network, and the target.</li><li>Connection fails with a bad password after rotation: trace CPM, Verify/Change/Reconcile, and dependencies.</li></ul><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Common mistake:</strong> Restarting CPM for a session problem. CPM does not build the user's RDP or SSH session.</div></div>","part":"p1","order":2,"duration":22,"level":"foundation","tags":["flow","PSM","CPM"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Gambar dua flow tanpa melihat materi","en":"Draw both flows from memory"},"brief":{"id":"Gambar session flow dan credential flow. Untuk setiap hop, tulis komponen, protocol, evidence, dan gejala jika hop gagal.","en":"Draw the session and credential flows. For every hop, record component, protocol, evidence, and failure symptom."},"deliverables":{"id":["Diagram session flow.","Diagram credential flow.","Tiga contoh salah diagnosis CPM vs PSM."],"en":["Session-flow diagram.","Credential-flow diagram.","Three CPM-versus-PSM misdiagnosis examples."]},"safety":{"id":"Tidak memerlukan akses production.","en":"No production access is required."}}},"m3":{"id":"m3","title":"Arsitektur dan Jalur Network","en":"Architecture and Network Paths","phase":"1. Dasar Sistem","phaseEn":"1. Core Mechanics","lead":"Memetakan Vault, PVWA, CPM, PSM, PSMP, PTA, serta dependency di sekitarnya.","leadEn":"Map Vault, PVWA, CPM, PSM, PSMP, PTA, and the dependencies around them.","objId":["Menjelaskan peran komponen utama","Memetakan source, destination, protocol, dan port","Membedakan masalah komponen dan dependency"],"objEn":["Explain each core component","Map source, destination, protocol, and port","Separate component and dependency failures"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Komponen inti</h2><table><tr><th>Komponen</th><th>Peran operasional</th></tr><tr><td>Digital Vault</td><td>Menyimpan account object, credential, policy, authorization, dan audit.</td></tr><tr><td>PVWA</td><td>Portal web untuk login, request, pencarian account, administration, dan API.</td></tr><tr><td>CPM</td><td>Melakukan Verify, Change, Reconcile, serta update usage/dependency bila dikonfigurasi.</td></tr><tr><td>PSM / PSMP</td><td>Mem-proxy session Windows, SSH, database, atau web tanpa membuka credential ke user.</td></tr><tr><td>PTA</td><td>Mengolah sinyal ancaman dan perilaku berisiko sesuai deployment.</td></tr></table><h3>Network matrix yang harus dimiliki L2</h3><p>Untuk setiap flow, catat source, destination, protocol, port, DNS name, proxy/load balancer, certificate, dan owner firewall. Port Vault yang sering dijumpai adalah TCP 1858, tetapi nilai aktual wajib diverifikasi pada deployment. Jalur target bergantung protokol: misalnya RDP 3389, SSH 22, HTTPS 443, atau port database.</p><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Praktik aman:</strong> Jangan menyimpulkan “network aman” hanya karena ping berhasil. Uji protocol dan port yang benar dari host sumber yang benar.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Core components</h2><table><tr><th>Component</th><th>Operational role</th></tr><tr><td>Digital Vault</td><td>Stores account objects, credentials, policy, authorization, and audit records.</td></tr><tr><td>PVWA</td><td>Web portal for sign-in, requests, account search, administration, and APIs.</td></tr><tr><td>CPM</td><td>Runs Verify, Change, Reconcile, and configured usage or dependency updates.</td></tr><tr><td>PSM / PSMP</td><td>Proxies Windows, SSH, database, or web sessions without exposing the credential to the user.</td></tr><tr><td>PTA</td><td>Processes threat and risky-behavior signals where deployed.</td></tr></table><h3>The network matrix an L2 engineer needs</h3><p>For every flow, record source, destination, protocol, port, DNS name, proxy or load balancer, certificate, and firewall owner. TCP 1858 is a commonly documented Vault communication default, but the actual deployment value must be verified. Target paths depend on protocol, such as RDP 3389, SSH 22, HTTPS 443, or database-specific ports.</p><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Safe practice:</strong> Do not declare the network healthy because ping works. Test the correct protocol and port from the correct source host.</div></div>","part":"p2","order":3,"duration":30,"level":"foundation","tags":["architecture","network","ports"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Bangun network matrix","en":"Build a network matrix"},"brief":{"id":"Buat matrix source, destination, DNS/FQDN, protocol, port, certificate, firewall owner, dan validation command untuk setiap flow.","en":"Create a matrix of source, destination, DNS/FQDN, protocol, port, certificate, firewall owner, and validation command for each flow."},"deliverables":{"id":["Matrix PVWA/Vault/CPM/PSM/target.","Daftar port yang version-dependent.","Working-path comparison."],"en":["PVWA/Vault/CPM/PSM/target matrix.","Version-dependent port list.","Working-path comparison."]},"safety":{"id":"Validasi port deployment; angka default bukan bukti konfigurasi aktual.","en":"Validate deployed ports; defaults are not proof of actual configuration."}}},"m4":{"id":"m4","title":"Safe dan Platform: Authorization vs Policy","en":"Safe and Platform: Authorization vs Policy","phase":"2. Administrasi","phaseEn":"2. Administration","lead":"Safe menentukan siapa boleh melakukan apa; Platform menentukan bagaimana account dikelola.","leadEn":"A Safe defines who can do what; a Platform defines how an account is managed.","objId":["Membedakan fungsi Safe dan Platform","Membaca permission efektif","Menghindari perubahan permission yang terlalu luas"],"objEn":["Separate Safe and Platform responsibilities","Read effective permissions","Avoid overly broad permission changes"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Safe menjawab “siapa boleh apa”</h2><p>Safe adalah boundary otorisasi dan penyimpanan logis. Membership memberi kemampuan terpisah, misalnya melihat daftar account, menggunakan account melalui Connect, mengambil atau menampilkan password, menambah account, mengelola member, atau melihat audit. Connect-only dan Show Password bukan hak yang sama.</p><h2>Platform menjawab “account ini dikelola bagaimana”</h2><p>Platform memuat aturan seperti plugin target, panjang dan kompleksitas password, interval Verify/Change, connection component, serta parameter lain yang bergantung versi. Satu Platform dapat dipakai banyak account; perubahan Platform karena itu dapat berdampak luas.</p><h3>Urutan cek saat tombol Connect hilang</h3><ol><li>Pastikan account benar-benar ada dan dapat dilihat user.</li><li>Periksa membership Safe dan permission efektif, termasuk group.</li><li>Periksa Platform dan connection component yang diizinkan.</li><li>Bandingkan dengan satu user atau account yang bekerja.</li></ol><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Jangan:</strong> Menambah seluruh permission hanya agar ticket cepat selesai. Perbaiki hak minimum yang memang hilang dan dokumentasikan approval-nya.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>A Safe answers “who may do what?”</h2><p>A Safe is a logical storage and authorization boundary. Membership grants separate capabilities, such as listing accounts, using an account through Connect, retrieving or displaying a password, adding accounts, managing members, or viewing audit. Connect-only access is not the same as Show Password access.</p><h2>A Platform answers “how is this account managed?”</h2><p>A Platform contains rules such as the target plugin, password length and complexity, Verify and Change intervals, connection-component mapping, and other version-dependent parameters. One Platform can serve many accounts, so a change can have a wide blast radius.</p><h3>When Connect is missing</h3><ol><li>Confirm the user can see the account object.</li><li>Check Safe membership and effective permissions, including group membership.</li><li>Check the Platform and permitted connection component.</li><li>Compare against one working user or account.</li></ol><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Do not:</strong> Grant every permission just to close the ticket. Restore only the missing least-privilege permission and record the approval.</div></div>","part":"p2","order":4,"duration":28,"level":"operator","tags":["Safe","Platform","RBAC"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Review permission matrix","en":"Review a permission matrix"},"brief":{"id":"Rancang Safe untuk operator connect-only, Safe manager, auditor, dan PAM admin. Bedakan Use, Retrieve, List, Audit, dan Manage Members.","en":"Design a Safe for connect-only operators, Safe managers, auditors, and PAM admins. Separate Use, Retrieve, List, Audit, and Manage Members."},"deliverables":{"id":["RBAC matrix.","Dua contoh excessive privilege.","Test case Connect works / Show Password denied."],"en":["RBAC matrix.","Two excessive-privilege examples.","Test case: Connect works / Show Password denied."]},"safety":{"id":"Perubahan permission produksi wajib approved change.","en":"Production permission changes require approved change control."}}},"m5":{"id":"m5","title":"CPM: Verify, Change, dan Reconcile","en":"CPM: Verify, Change, and Reconcile","phase":"2. Administrasi","phaseEn":"2. Administration","lead":"Memahami tiga operasi CPM, penyebab out-of-sync, dan risiko dependency.","leadEn":"Understand the three CPM operations, out-of-sync conditions, and dependency risk.","objId":["Membedakan Verify, Change, Reconcile","Menjelaskan fungsi Reconcile Account dan Logon Account","Menilai dampak service-account dependency"],"objEn":["Differentiate Verify, Change, and Reconcile","Explain Reconcile and Logon Accounts","Assess service-account dependencies"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Tiga operasi yang harus dibedakan</h2><table><tr><th>Operasi</th><th>Apa yang dilakukan</th><th>Petunjuk kegagalan</th></tr><tr><td>Verify</td><td>Menguji apakah credential di Vault dapat login ke target.</td><td>Network, authentication, policy target, atau password mismatch.</td></tr><tr><td>Change</td><td>Mengganti password menggunakan credential lama lalu menyimpan nilai baru.</td><td>Password policy, plugin prompt, hak account, atau target error.</td></tr><tr><td>Reconcile</td><td>Mereset password dengan account lain yang punya hak reset ketika password lama tidak dapat dipakai.</td><td>Reconcile Account, association, permission, atau target procedure.</td></tr></table><h3>Account pendukung</h3><p>Reconcile Account dipakai untuk reset paksa. Logon Account dapat dipakai sebagai account perantara sebelum masuk ke mode privileged pada target tertentu. Keduanya bukan pengganti managed account dan harus dibatasi.</p><h3>Dependency adalah bagian dari perubahan</h3><p>Jika password service account berubah, Windows Service, scheduled task, app pool, script, atau connection string yang memakai password lama juga perlu diperbarui. Status account bisa terlihat compliant sementara aplikasinya sudah gagal.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Checklist L2:</strong> timestamp operasi, account ID, Platform, CPM yang menangani, error exact, CPM log, target response, status Verify terakhir, dan daftar usage/dependency.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Three operations that must not be confused</h2><table><tr><th>Operation</th><th>What it does</th><th>Failure clues</th></tr><tr><td>Verify</td><td>Tests whether the credential stored in the Vault can authenticate to the target.</td><td>Network, authentication, target policy, or password mismatch.</td></tr><tr><td>Change</td><td>Changes the password with the current credential and stores the new value.</td><td>Password policy, plugin prompt, account rights, or target errors.</td></tr><tr><td>Reconcile</td><td>Resets the password through another account with reset rights when the old password cannot be used.</td><td>Reconcile Account, association, permissions, or target procedure.</td></tr></table><h3>Supporting accounts</h3><p>A Reconcile Account performs a forced reset. A Logon Account may provide an intermediate login before switching to privileged mode on certain targets. Neither replaces the managed account, and both require tight controls.</p><h3>Dependencies are part of the change</h3><p>After a service-account password changes, Windows Services, scheduled tasks, app pools, scripts, or connection strings using the old password may also need an update. The account can look compliant while the application is already down.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>L2 evidence set:</strong> operation timestamp, account ID, Platform, handling CPM, exact error, CPM log, target response, last Verify status, and all configured usages or dependencies.</div></div>","part":"p2","order":5,"duration":32,"level":"operator","tags":["CPM","Verify","Change","Reconcile"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Simulasi lifecycle CPM","en":"Simulate the CPM lifecycle"},"brief":{"id":"Untuk satu managed account, tulis precondition, action, expected result, log, dan recovery path untuk Verify, Change, dan Reconcile.","en":"For one managed account, document preconditions, actions, expected results, logs, and recovery paths for Verify, Change, and Reconcile."},"deliverables":{"id":["Lifecycle worksheet.","Dependency impact list.","Decision kapan Reconcile aman."],"en":["Lifecycle worksheet.","Dependency impact list.","Decision for when Reconcile is safe."]},"safety":{"id":"Jangan melakukan manual password change pada target dan Vault secara terpisah.","en":"Never change target and Vault passwords separately without an approved recovery procedure."}}},"m6":{"id":"m6","title":"Menemukan Log dan Menyusun Timeline","en":"Finding Logs and Building a Timeline","phase":"3. Troubleshooting L2","phaseEn":"3. L2 Troubleshooting","lead":"Memilih log berdasarkan flow, lalu mengorelasikan event dengan timestamp dan timezone.","leadEn":"Choose logs from the failing flow, then correlate events by timestamp and timezone.","objId":["Memilih log komponen yang relevan","Membangun timeline lintas komponen","Mengumpulkan evidence tanpa membocorkan secret"],"objEn":["Choose the relevant component logs","Build a cross-component timeline","Collect evidence without exposing secrets"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Log mengikuti komponen yang melakukan pekerjaan</h2><table><tr><th>Gejala</th><th>Mulai dari</th></tr><tr><td>PVWA error, login, API, IIS</td><td>PVWA application logs, IIS logs, Windows Event Viewer.</td></tr><tr><td>Verify, Change, Reconcile</td><td>CPM component logs dan response target.</td></tr><tr><td>Session gagal, disconnect, dispatcher</td><td>PSM/PSMP logs, AppLocker/Event Viewer, target protocol logs.</td></tr><tr><td>Authorization atau Vault connectivity</td><td>Vault audit/component evidence sesuai runbook dan kewenangan.</td></tr></table><p>Nama file dan path log dapat berubah menurut versi, build, dan arsitektur. Gunakan dokumentasi build customer dan runbook internal sebagai sumber kebenaran.</p><h3>Metode pencarian yang efisien</h3><ol><li>Catat waktu kejadian sampai detik, timezone, user, account, target, dan action.</li><li>Reproduksi sekali bila aman.</li><li>Cari correlation, session, request, atau account identifier.</li><li>Susun timeline dari portal ke komponen lalu target.</li><li>Bandingkan dengan satu flow yang berhasil.</li></ol><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Redaction:</strong> Jangan menaruh password, token, key, atau isi credential di ticket. Ambil error dan identifier yang diperlukan saja.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Logs follow the component doing the work</h2><table><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Start with</th></tr><tr><td>PVWA error, login, API, IIS</td><td>PVWA application logs, IIS logs, and Windows Event Viewer.</td></tr><tr><td>Verify, Change, Reconcile</td><td>CPM component logs and the target response.</td></tr><tr><td>Session failure, disconnect, dispatcher</td><td>PSM or PSMP logs, AppLocker or Event Viewer, and target protocol logs.</td></tr><tr><td>Authorization or Vault connectivity</td><td>Vault audit or component evidence permitted by the runbook and your role.</td></tr></table><p>File names and log paths can vary by version, build, and architecture. Treat the customer's build documentation and internal runbook as the source of truth.</p><h3>An efficient search method</h3><ol><li>Record the event time to the second, timezone, user, account, target, and action.</li><li>Reproduce once if it is safe.</li><li>Search correlation, session, request, or account identifiers.</li><li>Build a timeline from portal to component to target.</li><li>Compare with one successful flow.</li></ol><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Redaction:</strong> Never place passwords, tokens, keys, or credential values in a ticket. Capture only the required error and identifiers.</div></div>","part":"p3","order":6,"duration":30,"level":"operator","tags":["logs","timeline","evidence"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Susun timeline incident","en":"Build an incident timeline"},"brief":{"id":"Dari log dummy, susun timeline portal → component → target. Tulis fakta, hipotesis, dan gap evidence secara terpisah.","en":"Using dummy logs, build a portal → component → target timeline. Separate facts, hypotheses, and evidence gaps."},"deliverables":{"id":["Timeline dengan timezone.","Correlation identifiers.","Satu working comparison."],"en":["Timezone-aware timeline.","Correlation identifiers.","One working comparison."]},"safety":{"id":"Redact password, token, key, dan data customer.","en":"Redact passwords, tokens, keys, and customer data."}}},"m7":{"id":"m7","title":"SAML, LDAP, MFA, dan Authentication","en":"SAML, LDAP, MFA, and Authentication","phase":"3. Troubleshooting L2","phaseEn":"3. L2 Troubleshooting","lead":"Memisahkan kegagalan identity provider, PVWA, directory, certificate, dan waktu.","leadEn":"Separate identity-provider, PVWA, directory, certificate, and time failures.","objId":["Membaca flow SAML secara berurutan","Mendeteksi time drift dan certificate issue","Membedakan masalah satu user dan seluruh user"],"objEn":["Read the SAML flow in sequence","Detect time drift and certificate issues","Separate one-user and all-user failures"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Authentication adalah rantai, bukan satu tombol</h2><div class=\"diagram\">Browser → PVWA/SP → IdP → SAML assertion → PVWA → authorization</div><p>Redirect loop tidak otomatis berarti PVWA rusak. Assertion dapat ditolak karena Audience/Entity ID salah, Reply URL tidak cocok, NameID atau group claim berbeda, signature certificate tidak dipercaya, atau jam server tidak sinkron.</p><h3>Gunakan scope untuk mempercepat diagnosis</h3><ul><li>Satu user gagal: cek status user, group mapping, attribute/claim, lockout, dan assignment.</li><li>Semua user SAML gagal: cek IdP availability, certificate, metadata/configuration, URL, dan NTP.</li><li>LDAP gagal tetapi local CyberArk user berhasil: fokus pada bind, directory path, connectivity, certificate, atau mapping.</li></ul><h3>Evidence minimum</h3><p>Exact timestamp, username yang sudah disamarkan bila perlu, authentication method, URL, browser behavior, IdP event, PVWA authentication log, certificate thumbprint/expiry, dan time offset. Jangan meminta password user.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Aturan praktis:</strong> Untuk error “not yet valid” atau “expired”, periksa waktu dan timezone sebelum mengganti konfigurasi SAML.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Authentication is a chain, not a button</h2><div class=\"diagram\">Browser → PVWA/SP → IdP → SAML assertion → PVWA → authorization</div><p>A redirect loop does not automatically mean PVWA is broken. An assertion may be rejected because the Audience or Entity ID is wrong, the Reply URL differs, NameID or group claims do not match, the signing certificate is untrusted, or server clocks are out of sync.</p><h3>Use scope to speed up diagnosis</h3><ul><li>One user fails: check user state, group mapping, attributes or claims, lockout, and assignment.</li><li>All SAML users fail: check IdP availability, certificates, metadata or configuration, URLs, and NTP.</li><li>LDAP fails while a local CyberArk user works: focus on bind, directory path, connectivity, certificates, or mapping.</li></ul><h3>Minimum evidence</h3><p>Exact timestamp, appropriately masked username, authentication method, URL, browser behavior, IdP event, PVWA authentication log, certificate thumbprint and expiry, and time offset. Never request the user's password.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Practical rule:</strong> For “not yet valid” or “expired” errors, check time and timezone before editing SAML configuration.</div></div>","part":"p3","order":7,"duration":28,"level":"operator","tags":["SAML","LDAP","MFA"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Triage SAML redirect loop","en":"Triage a SAML redirect loop"},"brief":{"id":"Buat checklist exact timestamp, IdP event, PVWA log, claim mapping, certificate, audience, reply URL, dan NTP.","en":"Create a checklist covering exact timestamp, IdP event, PVWA log, claim mapping, certificate, audience, reply URL, and NTP."},"deliverables":{"id":["Authentication chain.","Scope one user vs all users.","Evidence request untuk identity team."],"en":["Authentication chain.","One-user versus all-user scope.","Evidence request for the identity team."]},"safety":{"id":"Jangan menangkap atau menempel SAML token lengkap.","en":"Do not capture or paste a full SAML token."}}},"m8":{"id":"m8","title":"PSM, Connection Component, dan AppLocker","en":"PSM, Connection Components, and AppLocker","phase":"3. Troubleshooting L2","phaseEn":"3. L2 Troubleshooting","lead":"Membedah session yang tidak mulai, disconnect cepat, atau diblokir policy aplikasi.","leadEn":"Break down sessions that fail to start, drop quickly, or are blocked by application control.","objId":["Mengikuti lifecycle session PSM","Mengenali dispatcher dan connection component","Membedakan network, target, dan AppLocker"],"objEn":["Trace the PSM session lifecycle","Recognize dispatchers and connection components","Separate network, target, and AppLocker failures"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Lifecycle session</h2><ol><li>User memilih Connect di PVWA.</li><li>Authorization dan account association diperiksa.</li><li>User diarahkan ke PSM atau PSMP yang sesuai.</li><li>Connection Component menjalankan dispatcher atau client protocol.</li><li>PSM mengambil credential secara terkontrol dan membuka koneksi ke target.</li><li>Session dimonitor, direkam, dan ditutup sesuai policy.</li></ol><h3>Gejala memberi petunjuk layer</h3><ul><li>Putus sebelum jendela aplikasi muncul: connection component, executable, AppLocker, atau prerequisite.</li><li>Jendela muncul lalu target menolak: network PSM-to-target, protocol, target service, credential, atau policy target.</li><li>Hanya satu target gagal: bandingkan target tersebut dengan target sehat pada Platform yang sama.</li><li>Semua target satu connection component gagal setelah patch: curigai shared dependency atau application-control rule.</li></ul><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Jangan langsung men-disable AppLocker.</strong> Ambil event deny, nama executable, publisher/hash/path, dan cocokkan dengan baseline yang disetujui. Perubahan allow-list harus melalui change control.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Session lifecycle</h2><ol><li>The user selects Connect in PVWA.</li><li>Authorization and account association are checked.</li><li>The user is directed to the appropriate PSM or PSMP.</li><li>The Connection Component starts its dispatcher or protocol client.</li><li>PSM retrieves the credential under control and opens the target connection.</li><li>The session is monitored, recorded, and closed according to policy.</li></ol><h3>Symptoms point to a layer</h3><ul><li>The session drops before the client window appears: investigate the connection component, executable, AppLocker, or prerequisites.</li><li>The client appears but the target rejects it: investigate PSM-to-target network, protocol, target service, credential, or target policy.</li><li>Only one target fails: compare it with a healthy target on the same Platform.</li><li>Every target using one connection component fails after a patch: suspect a shared dependency or application-control rule.</li></ul><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Do not simply disable AppLocker.</strong> Capture the deny event, executable, publisher or hash or path, and compare it with the approved baseline. Allow-list changes require change control.</div></div>","part":"p3","order":8,"duration":32,"level":"operator","tags":["PSM","PSMP","AppLocker"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Isolasi PSM disconnect","en":"Isolate a PSM disconnect"},"brief":{"id":"Bandingkan session yang gagal dengan session sehat. Pisahkan launch, dispatcher, AppLocker, credential retrieval, network, dan target authentication.","en":"Compare a failed session with a healthy one. Separate launch, dispatcher, AppLocker, credential retrieval, network, and target authentication."},"deliverables":{"id":["Symptom-to-layer matrix.","AppLocker evidence list.","Approved validation sequence."],"en":["Symptom-to-layer matrix.","AppLocker evidence list.","Approved validation sequence."]},"safety":{"id":"Jangan men-disable AppLocker global untuk testing.","en":"Do not disable AppLocker globally for testing."}}},"m9":{"id":"m9","title":"Blueprint Implementasi CyberArk","en":"CyberArk Implementation Blueprint","phase":"4. Implementasi","phaseEn":"4. Implementation","lead":"Dari discovery dan desain sampai pilot, rollout, handover, dan acceptance.","leadEn":"Move from discovery and design through pilot, rollout, handover, and acceptance.","objId":["Menyusun discovery yang dapat ditindaklanjuti","Memisahkan desain identity, network, account, dan operations","Menyiapkan pilot serta acceptance criteria"],"objEn":["Create actionable discovery output","Separate identity, network, account, and operations design","Prepare a pilot and acceptance criteria"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Implementasi dimulai sebelum instalasi</h2><ol><li><b>Discovery:</b> jenis account, jumlah, owner, target, protocol, dependency, regulasi, availability, dan use case.</li><li><b>Design:</b> arsitektur, sizing, Safe model, Platform model, RBAC, authentication, network matrix, certificate, logging, backup, dan DR.</li><li><b>Build:</b> prerequisite, server hardening, instalasi/connector, integration, dan baseline configuration.</li><li><b>Pilot:</b> mulai dari account representatif namun blast radius rendah.</li><li><b>Rollout:</b> batch kecil, komunikasi owner, rollback, dan validation.</li><li><b>Handover:</b> runbook, monitoring, backup evidence, support matrix, known errors, dan training.</li></ol><h3>Acceptance criteria harus terukur</h3><p>Contoh: user dapat login dengan MFA, hanya melihat Safe yang berhak, Connect bekerja tanpa menampilkan password, CPM Verify dan Change berhasil, dependency tetap sehat, audit masuk ke SIEM, failover diuji, dan tim operasi dapat menjalankan runbook.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Pilot yang baik:</strong> mencakup satu Windows account, satu Linux account, satu service account dengan dependency, satu approval flow, dan satu use case session recording.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Implementation starts before installation</h2><ol><li><b>Discovery:</b> account types, volume, owners, targets, protocols, dependencies, regulation, availability, and use cases.</li><li><b>Design:</b> architecture, sizing, Safe model, Platform model, RBAC, authentication, network matrix, certificates, logging, backup, and DR.</li><li><b>Build:</b> prerequisites, server hardening, installation or connectors, integrations, and baseline configuration.</li><li><b>Pilot:</b> begin with representative accounts that have a low blast radius.</li><li><b>Rollout:</b> use small batches, owner communication, rollback, and validation.</li><li><b>Handover:</b> provide runbooks, monitoring, backup evidence, support matrix, known errors, and training.</li></ol><h3>Acceptance criteria must be measurable</h3><p>Examples: users sign in with MFA, see only authorized Safes, Connect works without revealing the password, CPM Verify and Change succeed, dependencies remain healthy, audit reaches the SIEM, failover is tested, and operations staff can follow the runbook.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>A useful pilot:</strong> includes a Windows account, a Linux account, a service account with a dependency, an approval flow, and a recorded-session use case.</div></div>","part":"p4","order":9,"duration":38,"level":"implementation","tags":["discovery","design","pilot"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Rancang pilot implementasi","en":"Design an implementation pilot"},"brief":{"id":"Rancang pilot kecil yang mewakili Windows, Linux, service account, approval, recording, SIEM, backup, dan rollback.","en":"Design a small pilot representing Windows, Linux, service accounts, approval, recording, SIEM, backup, and rollback."},"deliverables":{"id":["Discovery questionnaire.","Acceptance criteria.","Pilot and rollback plan."],"en":["Discovery questionnaire.","Acceptance criteria.","Pilot and rollback plan."]},"safety":{"id":"Pilih account representatif dengan blast radius rendah.","en":"Choose representative accounts with a low blast radius."}}},"m10":{"id":"m10","title":"PAM Self-Hosted vs Privilege Cloud","en":"PAM Self-Hosted vs Privilege Cloud","phase":"4. Implementasi","phaseEn":"4. Implementation","lead":"Memahami ownership boundary, Connector, dan cara mengisolasi masalah hybrid.","leadEn":"Understand ownership boundaries, connectors, and hybrid fault isolation.","objId":["Membandingkan tanggung jawab deployment","Memahami peran Connector Management","Mengisolasi SaaS core, connector lokal, dan target"],"objEn":["Compare deployment responsibilities","Understand Connector Management","Separate SaaS core, local connector, and target failures"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Teknologinya mirip, ownership-nya berbeda</h2><p>Pada PAM Self-Hosted, customer biasanya mengoperasikan Vault, PVWA, CPM, PSM/PSMP, database atau storage terkait, certificate, patching, monitoring, backup, dan DR sesuai desain. Pada Privilege Cloud, layanan inti disediakan sebagai SaaS, tetapi connector atau session components, target internal, identity integration, proxy, DNS, firewall, dan sebagian certificate tetap berada pada sisi customer.</p><h3>Tiga boundary saat troubleshooting cloud</h3><ol><li><b>SaaS core:</b> portal, tenant behavior, cloud-side operation, service status, correlation ID.</li><li><b>Connector lokal:</b> health, service, prerequisite, upgrade, proxy/outbound TLS, certificate, dan log.</li><li><b>Target internal:</b> DNS, protocol port, authentication, policy, dan availability.</li></ol><p>Jika portal dapat dibuka tetapi semua operasi ke target internal berhenti, periksa health connector dan jalur connector-to-target sebelum menyimpulkan SaaS outage.</p><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Escalation boundary:</strong> Kumpulkan tenant, timestamp/timezone, connector identity, task/correlation ID, target scope, evidence lokal, dan hasil pembanding. Jangan mengirim credential.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Similar capabilities, different ownership</h2><p>In PAM Self-Hosted, the customer typically operates the Vault, PVWA, CPM, PSM or PSMP, related storage, certificates, patching, monitoring, backup, and DR according to the design. In Privilege Cloud, core services are delivered as SaaS, while connectors or session components, internal targets, identity integration, proxy, DNS, firewall, and some certificates remain customer-side responsibilities.</p><h3>Three troubleshooting boundaries in cloud</h3><ol><li><b>SaaS core:</b> portal, tenant behavior, cloud-side tasks, service status, and correlation IDs.</li><li><b>Local connector:</b> health, service, prerequisites, upgrade state, proxy or outbound TLS, certificates, and logs.</li><li><b>Internal target:</b> DNS, protocol port, authentication, policy, and availability.</li></ol><p>If the portal is available but all operations to internal targets stop, check connector health and the connector-to-target path before declaring a SaaS outage.</p><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Escalation boundary:</strong> Collect tenant, timestamp and timezone, connector identity, task or correlation ID, target scope, local evidence, and a working comparison. Never send credentials.</div></div>","part":"p4","order":10,"duration":28,"level":"implementation","tags":["Self-Hosted","Privilege Cloud","connector"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Buat ownership boundary","en":"Create an ownership boundary"},"brief":{"id":"Bandingkan SaaS core, connector lokal, target, IdP, proxy, DNS, firewall, dan certificate owner.","en":"Compare ownership for SaaS core, local connector, target, IdP, proxy, DNS, firewall, and certificates."},"deliverables":{"id":["RACI Self-Hosted vs Cloud.","Connector health checklist.","Escalation evidence package."],"en":["Self-Hosted versus Cloud RACI.","Connector health checklist.","Escalation evidence package."]},"safety":{"id":"Jangan menyimpulkan SaaS outage dari satu connector offline.","en":"Do not declare a SaaS outage from one offline connector."}}},"m11":{"id":"m11","title":"Reliability: Backup, RTO, dan Failover","en":"Reliability: Backup, RTO, and Failover","phase":"5. Operasi & SLA","phaseEn":"5. Operations & SLA","lead":"High availability untuk resilience, disaster recovery untuk survive.","leadEn":"High availability provides resilience; disaster recovery provides survival.","objId":["Membedakan High Availability dan Disaster Recovery","Menjelaskan konsep Recovery Time dan Point Objective","Mengisolasi komponen yang gagal secara aman"],"objEn":["Differentiate High Availability and Disaster Recovery","Explain Recovery Time and Point Objectives","Isolate failing components safely"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>HA mempertahankan SLA, DR menyelamatkan layanan</h2><p>CyberArk menyimpan rahasia paling penting perusahaan. Saat Vault atau komponen kehilangan koneksi, bisnis dapat lumpuh, incident response terhambat, atau SLA tim meleset. High availability pada komponen memastikan layanan langsung merutekan trafik jika terjadi node failure. Namun, jika ada data corruption, kehilangan site, atau incident parah, HA bisa saja merutekan kerusakan yang sama. Saat itulah DR diperlukan dengan data vaulting yang terlindungi.</p><h3>Syarat recovery yang sehat</h3><ul><li><b>Sync status:</b> data direplikasi secara rutin (misalnya pad dan failover DR vault).</li><li><b>RTO / RPO:</b> berapa lama layanan bisa mati, dan berapa banyak waktu data yang siap direlakan.</li><li><b>Validation:</b> memastikan operasi Verify, Change, RDP session, SSH session, dan audit berhasil sesudah failover. Jangan sekadar memastikan service running.</li></ul><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>Dalam situasi P1:</strong> Ikuti procedure emergency/approved plan, kumpulkan minimum evidence secara paralel, komunikasikan impact, dan jangan ambil tindakan disruptif tanpa bukti atau timestamp kejadian awal.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>HA maintains SLAs; DR saves the service</h2><p>CyberArk holds the enterprise's most critical secrets. When the Vault or a component drops connection, business stops, incident response is blocked, or team SLAs fail. High availability on components ensures traffic routes around a dead node immediately. However, if data corrupts, a site is lost, or a severe incident occurs, HA may just replicate the damage. That is when DR, with protected vaulting, takes over.</p><h3>Healthy recovery requirements</h3><ul><li><b>Sync status:</b> data is routinely replicated (for example, DR vault pad and failover files).</li><li><b>RTO / RPO:</b> how much downtime is permitted, and how much data loss is acceptable.</li><li><b>Validation:</b> verify that Verify, Change, RDP session, SSH session, and audit operations succeed after failover. Do not just confirm a service is running.</li></ul><div class=\"callout warning\"><strong>During a P1 event:</strong> Follow the emergency or approved procedure, collect minimum evidence in parallel, communicate impact, and do not take disruptive action without proof or the initial event timestamp.</div></div>","part":"p5","order":11,"duration":30,"level":"advanced","tags":["HA","DR","backup","RTO","RPO"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Tabletop HA/DR","en":"Run an HA/DR tabletop"},"brief":{"id":"Simulasikan node failure, site failure, dan data corruption. Tentukan kapan HA cukup dan kapan DR diperlukan.","en":"Simulate node failure, site failure, and data corruption. Decide when HA is sufficient and when DR is required."},"deliverables":{"id":["RTO/RPO statement.","Failover validation checklist.","Communication and rollback steps."],"en":["RTO/RPO statement.","Failover validation checklist.","Communication and rollback steps."]},"safety":{"id":"Vault failover/recovery hanya melalui authorized runbook.","en":"Vault failover and recovery must follow an authorized runbook."}}},"m12":{"id":"m12","title":"Identity, API, dan Integrations","en":"Identity, APIs, and Integrations","phase":"5. Reliability","phaseEn":"5. Reliability","lead":"Menghubungkan CyberArk dengan IdP, SIEM, ITSM, dan automation secara aman.","leadEn":"Connect CyberArk to IdPs, SIEM, ITSM, and automation without weakening controls.","objId":["Memetakan sumber kegagalan identity","Menetapkan boundary automation yang aman","Menjaga least privilege dan audit"],"objEn":["Map identity failure sources","Set safe automation boundaries","Preserve least privilege and audit"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Integrasi menambah dependency baru</h2><p>CyberArk jarang berdiri sendiri. Ticket dapat berasal dari AD/LDAP, SAML/IdP, MFA, load balancer, certificate authority, SIEM, ITSM, API client, atau target application.</p><table><tr><th>Integrasi</th><th>Clue yang sering muncul</th></tr><tr><td>LDAP / AD</td><td>Bind failure, group mapping salah, user locked, TLS trust.</td></tr><tr><td>SAML / IdP</td><td>Redirect loop, audience, NameID, claim, certificate, time.</td></tr><tr><td>REST API</td><td>Token, endpoint, TLS, permission, rate, object ID.</td></tr><tr><td>SIEM / ITSM</td><td>Event hilang, webhook gagal, timestamp tidak cocok.</td></tr></table><p>Automation harus memakai service identity, least privilege, secret rotation, error handling, dan audit. Password plaintext di script bukan automation; itu secret exposure yang menunggu terjadi.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Boundary L2:</strong> Pastikan apakah error terjadi sebelum request masuk CyberArk, di object authorization, saat component menjalankan action, atau saat event dikirim ke sistem eksternal.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Integrations add new dependencies</h2><p>CyberArk rarely stands alone. A ticket may originate in AD or LDAP, SAML or an IdP, MFA, a load balancer, a certificate authority, SIEM, ITSM, an API client, or the target application.</p><table><tr><th>Integration</th><th>Common clues</th></tr><tr><td>LDAP / AD</td><td>Bind failure, wrong group mapping, locked user, or TLS trust.</td></tr><tr><td>SAML / IdP</td><td>Redirect loop, audience, NameID, claims, certificates, or time.</td></tr><tr><td>REST API</td><td>Token, endpoint, TLS, permission, rate, or object ID.</td></tr><tr><td>SIEM / ITSM</td><td>Missing event, failed webhook, or mismatched timestamps.</td></tr></table><p>Automation needs a service identity, least privilege, secret rotation, error handling, and audit. A plaintext password in a script is not automation; it is secret exposure waiting to happen.</p><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>L2 boundary:</strong> Decide whether the error occurs before the request reaches CyberArk, during object authorization, while a component runs the action, or while an event is sent to an external system.</div></div>","part":"p5","order":12,"duration":30,"level":"advanced","tags":["API","SIEM","ITSM","identity"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Petakan integration failure","en":"Map an integration failure"},"brief":{"id":"Ambil satu API atau SIEM flow. Pisahkan client, DNS/proxy, TLS, authentication, authorization, component action, dan external delivery.","en":"Take one API or SIEM flow. Separate client, DNS/proxy, TLS, authentication, authorization, component action, and external delivery."},"deliverables":{"id":["Integration sequence diagram.","Service identity controls.","Failure-boundary checklist."],"en":["Integration sequence diagram.","Service-identity controls.","Failure-boundary checklist."]},"safety":{"id":"Tidak ada password plaintext di script atau note.","en":"No plaintext passwords in scripts or notes."}}},"m13":{"id":"m13","title":"Ticket Ownership dan RCA","en":"Ticket Ownership and RCA","phase":"6. L2 Mastery","phaseEn":"6. L2 Mastery","lead":"Membuat update ticket dan escalation package yang dapat ditindaklanjuti.","leadEn":"Write ticket updates and escalation packages that another engineer can act on.","objId":["Menulis update berbasis evidence","Menguji hipotesis tanpa membuat perubahan berbahaya","Mengekskalasi dengan pertanyaan spesifik"],"objEn":["Write evidence-based updates","Test hypotheses without unsafe changes","Escalate with a specific question"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>L2 bukan sekadar meneruskan ticket</h2><p>Ownership berarti kamu mengetahui dampak, scope, apa yang sudah diuji, dan apa yang masih belum diketahui. Jangan menulis “CyberArk error” tanpa menjelaskan flow yang gagal.</p><h3>Siklus penanganan</h3><ol><li>Konfirmasi impact dan priority.</li><li>Catat timestamp/timezone, user, account, target, dan frekuensi.</li><li>Buat satu atau dua hipotesis yang bisa dibuktikan.</li><li>Ambil evidence minimum dari komponen yang tepat.</li><li>Uji langkah aman dan dokumentasikan hasilnya.</li><li>Berikan workaround hanya jika approved.</li><li>Eskalasi dengan pertanyaan yang jelas: “Apakah error X pada build Y mengindikasikan Z?”</li></ol><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>RCA yang baik:</strong> bukan kalimat “karena network”, melainkan “CPM gagal membuka TCP ke target pada 14:05 UTC; koneksi dari host lain berhasil; firewall rule berubah pukul 14:03 UTC.”</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>L2 is more than forwarding a ticket</h2><p>Ownership means you know the impact, scope, tested actions, and remaining unknowns. Do not write “CyberArk error” without naming the failed flow.</p><h3>The handling cycle</h3><ol><li>Confirm impact and priority.</li><li>Record timestamp and timezone, user, account, target, and frequency.</li><li>Create one or two testable hypotheses.</li><li>Collect the smallest evidence set from the right component.</li><li>Test a safe action and document the result.</li><li>Offer a workaround only when approved.</li><li>Escalate with a clear question: “Does error X on build Y indicate Z?”</li></ol><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Good RCA:</strong> is not “the network is broken”; it is “CPM could not open TCP to the target at 14:05 UTC; another host succeeds; the firewall rule changed at 14:03 UTC.”</div></div>","part":"p6","order":13,"duration":30,"level":"mastery","tags":["ticket","RCA","escalation"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Tulis ticket dan RCA","en":"Write a ticket and RCA"},"brief":{"id":"Ubah ticket “CyberArk down” menjadi problem statement, scope, timeline, hypothesis, evidence, test, workaround, dan specific ask.","en":"Turn “CyberArk is down” into a problem statement, scope, timeline, hypothesis, evidence, tests, workaround, and specific ask."},"deliverables":{"id":["Customer update.","Internal technical note.","L3 escalation package."],"en":["Customer update.","Internal technical note.","L3 escalation package."]},"safety":{"id":"Pisahkan fakta, asumsi, dan tindakan yang belum approved.","en":"Separate facts, assumptions, and unapproved actions."}}},"m14":{"id":"m14","title":"Rencana Latihan 30–60–90 Hari","en":"The 30–60–90 Day Practice Plan","phase":"6. L2 Mastery","phaseEn":"6. L2 Mastery","lead":"Mengubah bacaan menjadi skill yang terlihat saat onboarding dan support.","leadEn":"Turn reading into visible skill during onboarding and support work.","objId":["Membuat deliberate practice loop","Menyiapkan pertanyaan onboarding","Mendefinisikan bukti kesiapan L2"],"objEn":["Create a deliberate practice loop","Prepare onboarding questions","Define evidence of L2 readiness"],"contentId":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Skill dibangun lewat pengulangan yang terukur</h2><table><tr><th>Periode</th><th>Fokus</th><th>Bukti</th></tr><tr><td>Hari 1–30</td><td>Shadow ticket, topology, glossary, log, policy.</td><td>Dapat menggambar dua flow dan memilih log awal.</td></tr><tr><td>Hari 31–60</td><td>Own kasus Verify/PSM/Safe dengan review.</td><td>Ticket update jelas dan evidence tidak berlebihan.</td></tr><tr><td>Hari 61–90</td><td>Own incident end-to-end, RCA, dan runbook.</td><td>Eskalasi tepat serta mampu memberi knowledge sharing.</td></tr></table><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Proof of mastery:</strong> Kamu dapat menjelaskan flow tanpa diagram, mengisolasi layer dari satu ticket, menjaga redaction, dan mengirim package L3 yang tidak dikembalikan karena evidence kurang.</div></div>","contentEn":"<div class=\"lesson-block\"><h2>Skill grows through measurable repetition</h2><table><tr><th>Period</th><th>Focus</th><th>Evidence</th></tr><tr><td>Days 1–30</td><td>Shadow tickets, topology, glossary, logs, and policy.</td><td>Draw both flows and choose the first log source.</td></tr><tr><td>Days 31–60</td><td>Own Verify, PSM, and Safe cases with review.</td><td>Write clear updates with a focused evidence set.</td></tr><tr><td>Days 61–90</td><td>Own incidents end to end, write RCA, and improve runbooks.</td><td>Escalate precisely and share repeatable knowledge.</td></tr></table><div class=\"callout safe\"><strong>Proof of mastery:</strong> You can explain the flow without a diagram, isolate a layer from one ticket, redact secrets, and send an L3 package that is not returned for missing evidence.</div></div>","part":"p6","order":14,"duration":24,"level":"mastery","tags":["onboarding","practice","roadmap"],"exercise":{"title":{"id":"Susun roadmap pribadi 90 hari","en":"Build a personal 90-day roadmap"},"brief":{"id":"Tentukan target minggu 1–4, 5–8, dan 9–12: shadowing, case ownership, playbook, certification, serta knowledge sharing.","en":"Set targets for weeks 1–4, 5–8, and 9–12: shadowing, case ownership, playbooks, certification, and knowledge sharing."},"deliverables":{"id":["Weekly learning target.","Ticket categories to master.","Proof-of-readiness checklist."],"en":["Weekly learning target.","Ticket categories to master.","Proof-of-readiness checklist."]},"safety":{"id":"Roadmap harus mengikuti access boundary dan review senior engineer.","en":"The roadmap must respect access boundaries and senior-engineer review."}}}},"questionBank":[{"m":"m1","q":{"id":"Saat user click \"Show Password\", aksi apa yang dicatat di Vault audit log?","en":"When a user clicks “Show Password”, which action is written to the Vault audit trail?"},"c":[{"id":"Retrieve Password","en":"Retrieve Password","correct":true},{"id":"Use Password","en":"Use Password","correct":false},{"id":"Change Password","en":"Change Password","correct":false},{"id":"Unlock Account","en":"Unlock Account","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Tombol Show/Copy Password menggunakan Retrieve Accounts permission, yang dicatat sebagai aksi retrieve di audit log.","en":"Showing or copying a password requires the relevant Retrieve Accounts permission and creates a retrieve event in the audit trail."}},{"m":"m1","q":{"id":"Port yang umum didokumentasikan sebagai default untuk komunikasi komponen ke Vault adalah...","en":"Which port is a commonly documented default for CPM-to-Vault communication?"},"c":[{"id":"443","en":"443","correct":false},{"id":"3389","en":"3389","correct":false},{"id":"1858","en":"1858","correct":true},{"id":"1433","en":"1433","correct":false}],"a":2,"e":{"id":"TCP 1858 umum dipakai untuk Vault protocol, tetapi nilai aktual harus diverifikasi pada desain dan build customer.","en":"TCP 1858 is commonly used for Vault protocol communication, but the deployed value must be confirmed in the customer design."}},{"m":"m2","q":{"id":"Jika server target Windows memblokir port 3389 dari IP server PSM, apa yang akan terjadi?","en":"If the Windows target blocks TCP 3389 from the PSM server, what is the likely symptom?"},"c":[{"id":"User tidak bisa mengakses PVWA","en":"The user cannot open PVWA","correct":false},{"id":"Tombol Connect hilang dari layar user","en":"Connect disappears from PVWA","correct":false},{"id":"Sesi RDP PSM muncul sebentar lalu disconnect","en":"The PSM RDP session appears and then disconnects","correct":true},{"id":"CPM gagal mengganti password","en":"CPM cannot change a password","correct":false}],"a":2,"e":{"id":"Tombol Connect ada di PVWA (berhasil). User rdp ke PSM (berhasil). Tapi saat PSM mencoba 3389 ke target, koneksi putus (disconnect).","en":"The user can reach PVWA and PSM, but PSM cannot complete the final RDP connection to the target."}},{"m":"m2","q":{"id":"{user} komplain password Linux tidak bisa diputar oleh CPM. Log apa yang paling utama untuk L2 periksa?","en":"A Linux password cannot be rotated by CPM. Which log is the first L2 source?"},"c":[{"id":"PVWA/IIS application logs","en":"PVWA or IIS logs","correct":false},{"id":"CPM component logs","en":"CPM component logs","correct":true},{"id":"PSM component/AppLocker logs","en":"PSM or AppLocker logs","correct":false},{"id":"Vault audit/component logs","en":"Only Vault audit logs","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"CPM (Password Manager) mengelola lifecycle credential; aktivitas rotasi harus dilacak pada CPM component logs untuk versi customer.","en":"CPM owns credential lifecycle operations. Use the CPM log and target response at the exact operation time."}},{"m":"m3","q":{"id":"Sebuah account berstatus “Verification Failed”. Apa arti operasional yang paling tepat?","en":"Operationally, what does “Verification Failed” usually indicate?"},"c":[{"id":"MFA user pasti gagal","en":"MFA failed for PVWA login","correct":false},{"id":"CPM tidak dapat memvalidasi credential ke target; penyebabnya bisa mismatch, network, permission, atau policy","en":"The Vault credential cannot authenticate to the target","correct":true},{"id":"PSM pasti gagal merekam","en":"PSM did not record the screen","correct":false},{"id":"Reconcile Account pasti terhapus","en":"The Reconcile Account was deleted","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Verify Failed membuktikan validasi ke target tidak berhasil, tetapi L2 tetap harus membaca CPM log dan target response untuk menentukan penyebab.","en":"Verify tests whether the Vault value can be used on the target; failure may be mismatch, access, network, or policy."}},{"m":"m3","q":{"id":"Kapan Reconcile Account digunakan oleh CPM?","en":"When is a Reconcile Account used?"},"c":[{"id":"Setiap kali password masa berlakunya habis","en":"Whenever a password expires","correct":false},{"id":"Saat user menekan tombol Connect","en":"When a user clicks Connect","correct":false},{"id":"Hanya ketika password lama sudah mismatch/hilang sehingga CPM butuh akun super untuk me-reset target","en":"When the old password cannot be used and a privileged reset path is required","correct":true},{"id":"Setiap malam sebagai backup","en":"Every night as a backup","correct":false}],"a":2,"e":{"id":"Reconcile adalah opsi reset paksa menggunakan akun pihak ketiga yang punya hak akses administrator/root di target.","en":"Reconcile uses a separate account with reset rights to recover an out-of-sync managed account."}},{"m":"m4","q":{"id":"Beberapa user SAML terjebak redirect loop. Apa penyebab paling umum yang sering terlewat dari sisi server?","en":"Several SAML users enter a redirect loop. What is an easy-to-miss server-side check?"},"c":[{"id":"NTP/time sync","en":"Time synchronization","correct":true},{"id":"PSM disk","en":"PSM disk size","correct":false},{"id":"Safe size","en":"Safe size","correct":false},{"id":"CPM reconcile","en":"CPM reconcile","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"SAML assertion memiliki timestamp validitas yang sempit; clock drift dapat membuat assertion ditolak.","en":"Clock drift can make a SAML assertion appear not yet valid or already expired."}},{"m":"m4","q":{"id":"Sistem target mengharuskan password dengan panjang 20 karakter. CyberArk CPM mencoba Change tapi terus ditolak target. Dimana L2 harus mengubah setting panjang password?","en":"Where should a target password length of 20 characters normally be defined?"},"c":[{"id":"Di Safe Properties","en":"Safe properties","correct":false},{"id":"Di User AD Properties","en":"AD user properties","correct":false},{"id":"Di Platform Management","en":"Platform Management","correct":true},{"id":"Di Vault italog","en":"Vault audit log","correct":false}],"a":2,"e":{"id":"Platform Management adalah tempat mendefinisikan rules operasional seperti password length, complexity, dan rotasi.","en":"Platform policy holds operational rules such as password length and complexity."}},{"m":"m5","q":{"id":"Apa perbedaan HA dan DR?","en":"What is the practical difference between HA and DR?"},"c":[{"id":"HA adalah monitoring, DR adalah logging","en":"HA is monitoring and DR is logging","correct":false},{"id":"HA menjaga layanan saat node gagal; DR memulihkan layanan setelah site/system disruption","en":"HA keeps service available after a node failure; DR restores service after a larger disruption","correct":true},{"id":"HA untuk user, DR untuk password","en":"HA is for users and DR is for passwords","correct":false},{"id":"Tidak ada perbedaan","en":"There is no difference","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"HA dan DR sama-sama reliability control, tetapi skenario dan prosedur recovery-nya berbeda.","en":"HA and DR both improve resilience, but they cover different failure scopes and recovery procedures."}},{"m":"m5","q":{"id":"Saat Privilege Cloud ticket muncul, boundary pertama yang perlu dipastikan adalah...","en":"For a Privilege Cloud ticket, what boundary should be checked first?"},"c":[{"id":"Apakah issue berada di SaaS core, connector lokal, atau target internal","en":"SaaS core, local connector, or internal target","correct":true},{"id":"Apakah user punya desktop wallpaper","en":"The user desktop wallpaper","correct":false},{"id":"Apakah Safe bernama benar saja","en":"Only the Safe name","correct":false},{"id":"Apakah password harus dihapus","en":"Whether the password should be deleted","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Cloud mengubah ownership boundary. Connector dan target lokal bisa tetap menjadi sumber masalah.","en":"Cloud changes ownership boundaries. The connector and internal target can still be the source of failure."}},{"m":"m6","q":{"id":"Mengapa exact timestamp penting dalam log analysis?","en":"Why is an exact timestamp important in log analysis?"},"c":[{"id":"Agar ticket terlihat panjang","en":"It makes the ticket longer","correct":false},{"id":"Karena component logs noisy dan perlu dikorelasikan terhadap satu event","en":"Noisy component logs must be correlated to one event","correct":true},{"id":"Agar user tidak menunggu","en":"It prevents the user from waiting","correct":false},{"id":"Karena password berubah setiap menit","en":"Passwords change every minute","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Timestamp dengan timezone memperkecil area pencarian dan membantu correlate antar PVWA/CPM/PSM/target.","en":"A timestamp with timezone reduces the search window and aligns PVWA, CPM, PSM, and target evidence."}},{"m":"m6","q":{"id":"Apa isi utama escalation package yang kuat?","en":"What belongs in a strong escalation package?"},"c":[{"id":"Hanya screenshot error","en":"Only an error screenshot","correct":false},{"id":"Problem, impact, topology, version, timestamps, evidence, steps tried, workaround, dan pertanyaan spesifik","en":"Problem, impact, topology, version, timestamp, evidence, steps tried, workaround, and a specific question","correct":true},{"id":"Password account","en":"The account password","correct":false},{"id":"Semua log tanpa redaction","en":"All logs without redaction","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"L3 perlu context dan proof, bukan dump data atau credential.","en":"L3 needs context and proof, not a credential or an unfiltered log dump."}},{"m":"m7","q":{"id":"Satu service account dipakai oleh Windows Service dan scheduled task. Apa risiko mengubah password tanpa usage update?","en":"A service account is used by a Windows Service and a scheduled task. What happens if the password changes without a usage update?"},"c":[{"id":"Dependency tetap memakai password lama sehingga service/task gagal","en":"The dependency keeps the old password and the service or task can fail","correct":true},{"id":"PSM otomatis menghapus service","en":"PSM deletes the service","correct":false},{"id":"PVWA berhenti","en":"PVWA stops","correct":false},{"id":"SAML certificate berubah","en":"The SAML certificate changes","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Credential rotation harus mempertimbangkan dependency update/usage sesuai design.","en":"Credential rotation must include the configured dependencies and their update method."}},{"m":"m7","q":{"id":"SAML assertion ditolak karena valid-from belum tercapai. Apa yang perlu dicek?","en":"A SAML assertion is rejected because its valid-from time has not arrived. What should be checked?"},"c":[{"id":"NTP/time sync","en":"NTP and time sync","correct":true},{"id":"PSM disk","en":"PSM disk","correct":false},{"id":"Safe size","en":"Safe size","correct":false},{"id":"CPM reconcile","en":"CPM reconcile","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Time drift antara PVWA dan IdP bisa membuat assertion dianggap belum valid atau sudah expired.","en":"Time drift between PVWA and the IdP can invalidate an otherwise correct assertion."}},{"m":"m8","q":{"id":"Dalam onboarding, mengapa initial Verify dilakukan?","en":"Why is initial Verify useful during onboarding?"},"c":[{"id":"Menguji user interface","en":"It tests the user interface","correct":false},{"id":"Memastikan password yang diinput dapat dipakai dari CPM ke target","en":"It proves CPM can use the entered credential against the target","correct":true},{"id":"Menghapus account lama","en":"It deletes the old account","correct":false},{"id":"Mengaktifkan PTA","en":"It enables PTA","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Verify memvalidasi credential dan connectivity sebelum account dipakai production.","en":"Verify validates credential and connectivity before the account is used in production."}},{"m":"m8","q":{"id":"Apa arti version-dependent dalam guidebook ini?","en":"What does “version-dependent” mean in this guide?"},"c":[{"id":"Semua materi tidak berguna","en":"The material is useless","correct":false},{"id":"Menu, log path, behavior, dan prosedur tertentu harus divalidasi terhadap build customer","en":"Menus, paths, behavior, and procedures must be validated against the customer build","correct":true},{"id":"Produk tidak punya dokumentasi","en":"The product has no documentation","correct":false},{"id":"Hanya berlaku untuk user baru","en":"It applies only to new users","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Mental model stabil, tetapi detail implementasi dapat berubah antar versi/deployment.","en":"The mental model is stable, while exact menus, paths, and behavior can vary across versions and deployments."}},{"m":"m9","q":{"id":"Apa tindakan paling aman ketika ada ticket P1 tetapi evidence belum lengkap?","en":"What is the safest action when a P1 ticket arrives but evidence is incomplete?"},"c":[{"id":"Langsung failover tanpa approval","en":"Fail over immediately without approval","correct":false},{"id":"Komunikasikan impact, kumpulkan minimum evidence paralel, ikuti emergency change/runbook","en":"Communicate impact, collect minimum evidence in parallel, and follow the approved emergency runbook","correct":true},{"id":"Hapus account","en":"Delete the account","correct":false},{"id":"Matikan logging","en":"Disable logging","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Urgency tidak menghapus governance. Gunakan emergency procedure yang approved dan tetap catat evidence.","en":"Urgency does not remove governance. Use the approved emergency path and keep an evidence trail."}},{"m":"m9","q":{"id":"Pada troubleshooting, scope “semua account di satu platform gagal” mengarah ke...","en":"All accounts on one Platform fail. What does that scope suggest?"},"c":[{"id":"Masalah random di satu target","en":"A random issue on one target","correct":false},{"id":"Platform/plugin/CPM path bersama yang perlu dibandingkan dengan working platform","en":"A shared Platform, plugin, or CPM path that should be compared with a working Platform","correct":true},{"id":"User password satu orang","en":"One user password","correct":false},{"id":"Satu Safe permission user","en":"One Safe permission","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Scope luas di satu platform menunjuk dependency bersama, bukan satu credential individual.","en":"A shared scope points to a common dependency rather than one credential."}},{"m":"m10","q":{"id":"Mengapa script automation tidak boleh menaruh password plaintext?","en":"Why should an automation script never contain a plaintext password?"},"c":[{"id":"Tidak ada alasan","en":"There is no reason","correct":false},{"id":"Itu memperbesar secret exposure dan merusak audit/rotation control","en":"It increases secret exposure and bypasses audit and rotation controls","correct":true},{"id":"Agar script lebih cepat","en":"It makes the script faster","correct":false},{"id":"Karena PVWA melarang semua API","en":"PVWA blocks all APIs","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Gunakan service identity, vault/API secret handling, least privilege, dan audit.","en":"Use a service identity, controlled secret retrieval, least privilege, and audit."}},{"m":"m10","q":{"id":"Apa tujuan last known good?","en":"What is the purpose of a last known good point?"},"c":[{"id":"Menentukan user paling senior","en":"Find the most senior user","correct":false},{"id":"Menentukan titik pembanding sebelum recent change atau regression","en":"Compare the current failure with the last successful state before a change or regression","correct":true},{"id":"Menentukan password berikutnya","en":"Choose the next password","correct":false},{"id":"Mengganti SLA","en":"Replace the SLA","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Last known good membantu memisahkan initial misconfiguration dari regression.","en":"The last known good state helps separate an initial misconfiguration from a regression after a change."}},{"m":"m11","q":{"id":"Setelah failover, validasi mana yang paling kuat?","en":"After failover, which validation is strongest?"},"c":[{"id":"Service berstatus Running saja","en":"Only confirm services are Running","correct":false},{"id":"Uji login, Verify/Change, session, dan audit end-to-end","en":"Test login, Verify/Change, sessions, and audit end to end","correct":true},{"id":"Ping server DR","en":"Ping the DR server","correct":false},{"id":"Tutup incident langsung","en":"Close the incident immediately","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Recovery harus membuktikan flow bisnis, bukan hanya status service.","en":"Recovery must prove business flows, not only service status."}},{"m":"m11","q":{"id":"Apa yang dijelaskan RPO?","en":"What does RPO describe?"},"c":[{"id":"Batas kehilangan data yang dapat diterima","en":"The acceptable amount of data loss","correct":true},{"id":"Jumlah user PSM","en":"The number of PSM users","correct":false},{"id":"Panjang password","en":"Password length","correct":false},{"id":"Waktu response helpdesk","en":"Helpdesk response time","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"RPO berhubungan dengan titik pemulihan data; RTO berhubungan dengan lama pemulihan layanan.","en":"RPO concerns the recoverable data point; RTO concerns service recovery time."}},{"m":"m12","q":{"id":"API request gagal sebelum mencapai CyberArk. Layer pertama yang dicek?","en":"An API request fails before reaching CyberArk. Which layer comes first?"},"c":[{"id":"Client, DNS/proxy, TLS, dan endpoint","en":"Client, DNS or proxy, TLS, and endpoint","correct":true},{"id":"CPM Reconcile","en":"CPM Reconcile","correct":false},{"id":"PSM recording","en":"PSM recording","correct":false},{"id":"Safe retention","en":"Safe retention","correct":false}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Tentukan dahulu apakah request sampai ke service sebelum memeriksa object authorization.","en":"First prove whether the request reaches the service before checking object authorization."}},{"m":"m12","q":{"id":"Kontrol minimum untuk automation yang aman?","en":"What is the minimum control set for safe automation?"},"c":[{"id":"Password plaintext dan admin penuh","en":"Plaintext password and full admin","correct":false},{"id":"Service identity, least privilege, rotation, error handling, audit","en":"Service identity, least privilege, rotation, error handling, and audit","correct":true},{"id":"Disable logging","en":"Disable logging","correct":false},{"id":"Shared personal account","en":"Shared personal account","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Automation tidak boleh menghilangkan lifecycle dan audit secret.","en":"Automation must preserve secret lifecycle and audit."}},{"m":"m13","q":{"id":"Kalimat RCA mana yang paling kuat?","en":"Which RCA statement is strongest?"},"c":[{"id":"Network bermasalah","en":"The network was broken","correct":false},{"id":"CPM timeout ke target 14:05 UTC setelah firewall rule berubah 14:03 UTC","en":"CPM timed out to the target at 14:05 UTC after a firewall rule changed at 14:03 UTC","correct":true},{"id":"CyberArk error","en":"CyberArk error","correct":false},{"id":"Sudah restart","en":"Restarted it","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"RCA yang kuat menyebut komponen, waktu, bukti, dan perubahan yang berkorelasi.","en":"A strong RCA names the component, time, evidence, and correlated change."}},{"m":"m13","q":{"id":"Apa tujuan pertanyaan spesifik saat eskalasi?","en":"Why include a specific question in an escalation?"},"c":[{"id":"Membuat ticket lebih panjang","en":"To make the ticket longer","correct":false},{"id":"Menjelaskan keputusan atau keahlian apa yang dibutuhkan dari L3","en":"To state which decision or expertise is needed from L3","correct":true},{"id":"Mengirim semua log","en":"To send every log","correct":false},{"id":"Menghindari ownership","en":"To avoid ownership","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Eskalasi harus menunjukkan apa yang sudah dibuktikan L2 dan apa yang masih perlu dijawab.","en":"Escalation should state what L2 proved and what remains unanswered."}},{"m":"m14","q":{"id":"Bukti kesiapan L2 pada 60–90 hari adalah...","en":"Evidence of L2 readiness by days 60–90 is..."},"c":[{"id":"Menghafal semua menu","en":"Memorizing every menu","correct":false},{"id":"Mengisolasi flow, menjaga redaction, menulis RCA, dan eskalasi lengkap","en":"Isolating flows, preserving redaction, writing RCA, and escalating completely","correct":true},{"id":"Selalu restart service","en":"Always restarting services","correct":false},{"id":"Menutup ticket tanpa review","en":"Closing tickets without review","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Kesiapan terlihat dari reasoning dan kualitas evidence, bukan hafalan menu.","en":"Readiness is demonstrated by reasoning and evidence quality, not menu memorization."}},{"m":"m14","q":{"id":"Pola belajar harian yang paling efektif?","en":"Which daily learning pattern is most effective?"},"c":[{"id":"Baca banyak tanpa latihan","en":"Read a lot without practice","correct":false},{"id":"Baca singkat, recall, kerjakan soal, lalu catat gap","en":"Read briefly, recall, answer questions, then record gaps","correct":true},{"id":"Tunggu semua training selesai","en":"Wait until all training is complete","correct":false},{"id":"Hanya menyalin runbook","en":"Only copy the runbook","correct":false}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Loop singkat dan konsisten membangun retrieval serta troubleshooting reflex.","en":"A short, consistent loop builds retrieval and troubleshooting reflexes."}},{"m":"m1","q":{"id":"Kontrol PAM mana yang paling langsung mengurangi shared-password risk?","en":"Which PAM control most directly reduces shared-password risk?"},"c":[{"id":"Vault + personal identity + audit","en":"Vault + personal identity + audit"},{"id":"Ping target","en":"Ping the target"},{"id":"Desktop wallpaper","en":"Desktop wallpaper"},{"id":"Disable logging","en":"Disable logging"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"PAM memisahkan personal identity dari credential privileged dan menambahkan audit.","en":"PAM separates personal identity from the privileged credential and adds audit."}},{"m":"m2","q":{"id":"Jika Connect tidak muncul, apakah CPM harus menjadi cek pertama?","en":"If Connect is missing, should CPM be the first check?"},"c":[{"id":"Ya selalu","en":"Always"},{"id":"Tidak; mulai dari authorization, Platform, dan connection component","en":"No; start with authorization, Platform, and connection component"},{"id":"Hapus account","en":"Delete the account"},{"id":"Restart Vault","en":"Restart Vault"}],"a":1,"e":{"id":"Connect adalah session entitlement; CPM mengelola credential lifecycle.","en":"Connect is a session entitlement; CPM manages credential lifecycle."}},{"m":"m3","q":{"id":"Kenapa ping sukses belum membuktikan protocol sehat?","en":"Why does a successful ping not prove a protocol is healthy?"},"c":[{"id":"Ping bukan test TCP/protocol dari source yang benar","en":"Ping is not a TCP/protocol test from the correct source"},{"id":"Ping selalu salah","en":"Ping is always wrong"},{"id":"Karena Vault tidak punya network","en":"Because Vault has no network"},{"id":"Karena DNS tidak penting","en":"Because DNS is irrelevant"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"L2 harus menguji protocol dan port dari host sumber yang melakukan flow.","en":"L2 must test the protocol and port from the host performing the flow."}},{"m":"m4","q":{"id":"User login tetapi tidak melihat account. Layer pertama?","en":"User signs in but sees no accounts. First layer?"},"c":[{"id":"Safe membership/List Accounts","en":"Safe membership/List Accounts"},{"id":"CPM reconcile","en":"CPM reconcile"},{"id":"PSM recording","en":"PSM recording"},{"id":"RDP client","en":"RDP client"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Authentication dan Safe authorization adalah layer terpisah.","en":"Authentication and Safe authorization are separate layers."}},{"m":"m5","q":{"id":"Apa risiko Reconcile pada service account tanpa dependency check?","en":"What is the risk of reconciling a service account without dependency checks?"},"c":[{"id":"Aplikasi dapat tetap memakai password lama dan gagal","en":"The application may keep the old password and fail"},{"id":"PSM hilang","en":"PSM disappears"},{"id":"SAML berubah","en":"SAML changes"},{"id":"Tidak ada risiko","en":"No risk"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Credential recovery harus mempertimbangkan service, task, app, dan script yang bergantung.","en":"Credential recovery must consider dependent services, tasks, apps, and scripts."}},{"m":"m6","q":{"id":"Evidence mana yang paling membantu mempersempit log search?","en":"Which evidence best narrows a log search?"},"c":[{"id":"Exact timestamp + timezone + correlation ID","en":"Exact timestamp + timezone + correlation ID"},{"id":"Warna browser","en":"Browser color"},{"id":"Nama project saja","en":"Project name only"},{"id":"Password","en":"Password"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Timestamp dan identifier membantu korelasi antar komponen tanpa menempelkan secret.","en":"Timestamp and identifiers correlate components without exposing secrets."}},{"m":"m7","q":{"id":"SAML NotBefore belum tercapai paling awal mengarah ke…","en":"SAML NotBefore has not arrived; what should you check first?"},"c":[{"id":"NTP/time drift","en":"NTP/time drift"},{"id":"Safe size","en":"Safe size"},{"id":"CPM plugin","en":"CPM plugin"},{"id":"PSM disk","en":"PSM disk"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Clock drift dapat membuat assertion dianggap belum valid.","en":"Clock drift can make the assertion appear not yet valid."}},{"m":"m8","q":{"id":"AppLocker deny pada dispatcher mengarah ke layer…","en":"An AppLocker deny on a dispatcher points to which layer?"},"c":[{"id":"Connection component/application control","en":"Connection component/application control"},{"id":"Safe membership","en":"Safe membership"},{"id":"Reconcile account","en":"Reconcile account"},{"id":"SIEM dashboard","en":"SIEM dashboard"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"PSM perlu menjalankan executable connection component yang dapat diblokir policy aplikasi.","en":"PSM must run a connection-component executable that application control can block."}},{"m":"m9","q":{"id":"Pilot implementasi yang baik harus punya apa?","en":"What should a good implementation pilot include?"},"c":[{"id":"Representative accounts + acceptance + rollback","en":"Representative accounts + acceptance + rollback"},{"id":"Mass onboarding tanpa owner","en":"Mass onboarding without owners"},{"id":"Production change tanpa approval","en":"Unapproved production change"},{"id":"Hanya screenshot","en":"Screenshots only"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Pilot menurunkan blast radius sambil menguji flow end-to-end.","en":"A pilot lowers blast radius while testing the end-to-end flow."}},{"m":"m10","q":{"id":"Pada Privilege Cloud, siapa yang sering tetap memiliki target internal dan connector?","en":"In Privilege Cloud, who often still owns internal targets and connectors?"},"c":[{"id":"Customer operations","en":"Customer operations"},{"id":"Tidak ada owner","en":"No one"},{"id":"End user personal account","en":"The end user personal account"},{"id":"SIEM saja","en":"SIEM only"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Cloud core mengubah ownership, tetapi connector dan target internal tetap boundary customer.","en":"Cloud core changes ownership, but connectors and internal targets remain a customer boundary."}},{"m":"m11","q":{"id":"Validasi DR paling kuat adalah…","en":"The strongest DR validation is…"},"c":[{"id":"End-to-end business flow + audit","en":"End-to-end business flow + audit"},{"id":"Service Running saja","en":"Only service status"},{"id":"Ping saja","en":"Ping only"},{"id":"Skip validation","en":"Skip validation"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Recovery harus membuktikan operasi yang dibutuhkan user dan audit.","en":"Recovery must prove required user operations and audit."}},{"m":"m12","q":{"id":"Automation secret sebaiknya…","en":"An automation secret should…"},"c":[{"id":"Dikelola lewat service identity dan vault/API control","en":"Use service identity and vault/API controls"},{"id":"Disimpan plaintext","en":"Be stored plaintext"},{"id":"Dikirim lewat chat","en":"Be sent over chat"},{"id":"Dipakai oleh semua user","en":"Be shared by all users"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Least privilege, rotation, error handling, dan audit adalah control minimum.","en":"Least privilege, rotation, error handling, and audit are minimum controls."}},{"m":"m13","q":{"id":"Specific ask dalam escalation package berguna untuk…","en":"Why include a specific ask in an escalation package?"},"c":[{"id":"Menunjukkan keputusan yang dibutuhkan L3","en":"State the decision needed from L3"},{"id":"Menghindari ownership","en":"Avoid ownership"},{"id":"Mengirim semua data","en":"Send all data"},{"id":"Menambah panjang ticket","en":"Make the ticket longer"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"L3 perlu tahu apa yang sudah dibuktikan dan pertanyaan apa yang tersisa.","en":"L3 needs to know what was proven and what remains unanswered."}},{"m":"m14","q":{"id":"Proof of L2 readiness yang paling kuat adalah…","en":"The strongest proof of L2 readiness is…"},"c":[{"id":"Scope, evidence, safe test, RCA, escalation lengkap","en":"Scope, evidence, safe test, RCA, complete escalation"},{"id":"Hafal semua menu","en":"Memorize every menu"},{"id":"Selalu restart service","en":"Always restart services"},{"id":"Tidak pernah eskalasi","en":"Never escalate"}],"a":0,"e":{"id":"Kesiapan L2 terlihat dari reasoning dan kualitas ownership.","en":"L2 readiness is demonstrated by reasoning and ownership quality."}}],"cases":{"cas1":{"id":{"title":"PSM Disconnect dalam 3 Detik","cat":"Session / PSM","desc":"User dapat menekan Connect, tetapi window RDP menutup sekitar tiga detik kemudian.","evi":["PVWA berhasil membuat request session.","Account lain pada PSM yang sama juga mulai terdampak.","Ada AppLocker deny untuk executable dispatcher setelah patch."],"hyp":"Dispatcher connection component diblokir AppLocker; Safe dan CPM bukan layer utama.","choices":["Korelasikan event AppLocker dan PSM log pada timestamp yang sama.","Restart semua service CyberArk tanpa mengambil log.","Lakukan Reconcile password target."],"correct":0,"invest":["Catat session/request ID dan waktu putus.","Cari executable serta rule deny di AppLocker/Event Viewer.","Bandingkan file/rule dengan baseline connection component.","Uji perubahan allow-list hanya melalui approved change.","Validasi recording dan koneksi target setelah perbaikan."],"avoid":"Men-disable AppLocker secara global.","esc":"Rule baseline atau executable vendor membutuhkan validasi L3/vendor."},"en":{"title":"PSM Disconnects After Three Seconds","cat":"Session / PSM","desc":"The user can select Connect, but the RDP window closes after roughly three seconds.","evi":["PVWA successfully creates a session request.","Other accounts using the same PSM are now affected.","An AppLocker deny for the dispatcher appears after a patch."],"hyp":"The connection-component dispatcher is blocked by AppLocker; Safe and CPM are not the primary layer.","choices":["Correlate the AppLocker event with the PSM log at the same timestamp.","Restart every CyberArk service before collecting logs.","Reconcile the target password."],"correct":0,"invest":["Record the session or request ID and disconnect time.","Find the executable and deny rule in AppLocker or Event Viewer.","Compare the file and rule with the approved connection-component baseline.","Test an allow-list change only through approved change control.","Validate recording and target connectivity after the fix."],"avoid":"Disabling AppLocker globally.","esc":"The baseline rule or vendor executable requires L3 or vendor validation."}},"cas2":{"id":{"title":"CPM Reconcile Gagal Berulang","cat":"Credential / CPM","desc":"Account out-of-sync. Verify dan Change gagal; Reconcile juga tidak berhasil.","evi":["Target dapat diakses dari host CPM.","Reconcile Account sendiri dapat login.","Error muncul setelah Platform parameter diubah."],"hyp":"Association atau procedure Reconcile pada Platform tidak cocok dengan target.","choices":["Ambil CPM log pada job Reconcile dan bandingkan Platform dengan versi working.","Ganti password manual tanpa approval.","Restart PSM."],"correct":0,"invest":["Catat account ID, Platform, CPM, dan timestamp.","Validasi association Reconcile Account tanpa menampilkan password.","Baca target response dan prompt sequence pada log.","Bandingkan parameter/plugin dengan Platform yang bekerja.","Uji satu perubahan yang approved lalu Verify ulang."],"avoid":"Mengubah password target dan Vault secara terpisah.","esc":"Plugin atau prompt target membutuhkan perubahan connector yang belum tervalidasi."},"en":{"title":"CPM Reconcile Fails Repeatedly","cat":"Credential / CPM","desc":"The account is out of sync. Verify and Change fail, and Reconcile also cannot recover it.","evi":["The target is reachable from the CPM host.","The Reconcile Account can authenticate.","The error started after a Platform parameter changed."],"hyp":"The Platform association or Reconcile procedure no longer matches the target.","choices":["Capture the CPM Reconcile job and compare the Platform with a working version.","Change the password manually without approval.","Restart PSM."],"correct":0,"invest":["Record account ID, Platform, CPM, and timestamp.","Validate the Reconcile Account association without revealing passwords.","Read the target response and prompt sequence in the log.","Compare parameters or plugin behavior with a working Platform.","Test one approved change and run Verify again."],"avoid":"Changing the target and Vault passwords separately.","esc":"The target prompt or plugin requires an unvalidated connector change."}},"cas3":{"id":{"title":"SAML Login Redirect Loop","cat":"Identity / SAML","desc":"Setelah autentikasi IdP berhasil, browser kembali ke halaman login PVWA terus-menerus.","evi":["Local CyberArk user dapat login.","IdP mencatat authentication success.","Waktu PVWA berbeda 95 detik dari IdP."],"hyp":"Assertion ditolak karena time drift, bukan karena password user atau Safe permission.","choices":["Bandingkan timestamp IdP dan PVWA lalu periksa NTP.","Reset password Domain Admin.","Reconcile semua account."],"correct":0,"invest":["Catat exact timestamp dan URL redirect.","Periksa PVWA authentication log dan IdP event.","Bandingkan NotBefore/NotOnOrAfter dengan clock server.","Perbaiki time sync melalui owner yang berwenang.","Uji satu user lalu kelompok user yang terdampak."],"avoid":"Mengubah metadata SAML sebelum membuktikan penyebab.","esc":"Waktu sudah sinkron tetapi signature, audience, atau claim tetap ditolak."},"en":{"title":"SAML Login Redirect Loop","cat":"Identity / SAML","desc":"After successful IdP authentication, the browser repeatedly returns to the PVWA login page.","evi":["A local CyberArk user can sign in.","The IdP records authentication success.","PVWA time differs from the IdP by 95 seconds."],"hyp":"The assertion is rejected because of time drift, not the user password or Safe permission.","choices":["Compare IdP and PVWA timestamps and check NTP.","Reset the Domain Admin password.","Reconcile every account."],"correct":0,"invest":["Record the exact timestamp and redirect URL.","Check PVWA authentication logs and the IdP event.","Compare NotBefore and NotOnOrAfter with the server clock.","Have the authorized owner correct time synchronization.","Test one user, then the affected group."],"avoid":"Editing SAML metadata before proving the cause.","esc":"Time is synchronized but signature, audience, or claims are still rejected."}},"cas4":{"id":{"title":"Sertifikat PVWA Kedaluwarsa","cat":"Web / TLS","desc":"Browser memberi TLS warning dan API client berhenti, sementara IIS masih merespons.","evi":["FQDN tidak berubah.","Sertifikat kedaluwarsa malam sebelumnya.","Beberapa integration flow ikut gagal."],"hyp":"IIS binding atau certificate chain tidak lagi valid; Safe dan CPM bukan sumber utama.","choices":["Periksa subject/SAN, expiry, chain, trust, dan IIS binding.","Hapus account dari Safe.","Restart Vault tanpa change."],"correct":0,"invest":["Validasi certificate dari sisi client dan server.","Periksa HTTPS binding serta application/event log.","Ikuti renewal procedure dan siapkan rollback.","Uji browser, API, SAML, dan component communication."],"avoid":"Mengganti certificate tanpa mencatat private-key access dan chain.","esc":"Certificate baru benar tetapi trust atau mutual TLS masih gagal."},"en":{"title":"Expired PVWA Certificate","cat":"Web / TLS","desc":"Browsers show a TLS warning and API clients stop, while IIS still responds.","evi":["The FQDN did not change.","The certificate expired the previous night.","Several integration flows also fail."],"hyp":"The IIS binding or certificate chain is invalid; Safe and CPM are not the primary cause.","choices":["Check subject/SAN, expiry, chain, trust, and IIS binding.","Delete the account from its Safe.","Restart the Vault without change control."],"correct":0,"invest":["Validate the certificate from client and server perspectives.","Check HTTPS binding and application or event logs.","Follow the renewal procedure and prepare rollback.","Test browser, API, SAML, and component communication."],"avoid":"Replacing a certificate without tracking private-key access and the full chain.","esc":"The new certificate is correct but trust or mutual TLS still fails."}},"cas5":{"id":{"title":"Rotasi Service Account Memutus Aplikasi","cat":"Dependency / CPM","desc":"CPM Change sukses dan account compliant, tetapi aplikasi tidak dapat start sesudahnya.","evi":["Password target sudah berubah.","Aplikasi masih memakai password lama.","Account memiliki usage/dependency."],"hyp":"Credential lifecycle berhasil, tetapi dependency update gagal atau definisinya tidak lengkap.","choices":["Inventaris semua usage lalu korelasikan CPM usage log dengan waktu perubahan.","Kembalikan password lewat chat ke tim aplikasi.","Restart PVWA."],"correct":0,"invest":["Identifikasi service, task, app pool, script, dan connection string.","Periksa configuration serta log update usage.","Tentukan owner dan maintenance window.","Uji satu dependency secara approved.","Validasi health aplikasi dan compliance account."],"avoid":"Membagikan password baru secara manual.","esc":"Custom application membutuhkan plugin atau atomic update yang belum didukung."},"en":{"title":"Service-Account Rotation Breaks an Application","cat":"Dependency / CPM","desc":"CPM Change succeeds and the account is compliant, but the application cannot start afterward.","evi":["The target password changed.","The application still uses the old password.","The account has a usage or dependency list."],"hyp":"Credential lifecycle succeeded, but the dependency update failed or is incomplete.","choices":["Inventory every usage and correlate the CPM usage log with the change time.","Send the new password to the application team over chat.","Restart PVWA."],"correct":0,"invest":["Identify services, tasks, app pools, scripts, and connection strings.","Review usage configuration and update logs.","Confirm the owner and maintenance window.","Test one approved dependency update.","Validate application health and account compliance."],"avoid":"Sharing the new password manually.","esc":"A custom application requires an unsupported plugin or atomic update."}},"cas6":{"id":{"title":"Privilege Cloud Connector Offline","cat":"Privilege Cloud","desc":"Portal dapat dibuka, tetapi Connect dan password management ke target internal berhenti.","evi":["SaaS portal tersedia.","Connector health menunjukkan offline.","Target internal tersedia dari network customer."],"hyp":"Masalah berada pada local connector service/lifecycle/network, bukan object Safe.","choices":["Periksa Connector Management, service lokal, outbound TLS/proxy, upgrade, dan log.","Hapus Safe lalu buat ulang.","Ubah password target manual."],"correct":0,"invest":["Buka health dan prerequisite result.","Korelasikan connector log dengan failed task.","Periksa service, DNS, proxy, certificate, dan outbound path.","Periksa connector-to-target protocol.","Validasi satu task setelah recovery."],"avoid":"Menganggap seluruh SaaS outage hanya dari satu connector offline.","esc":"Health connector normal tetapi task cloud gagal dengan correlation ID yang konsisten."},"en":{"title":"Privilege Cloud Connector Offline","cat":"Privilege Cloud","desc":"The portal is available, but Connect and password management to internal targets stop.","evi":["The SaaS portal is available.","Connector health shows offline.","The internal target is available inside the customer network."],"hyp":"The issue is in the local connector service, lifecycle, or network—not the Safe object.","choices":["Check Connector Management, local service, outbound TLS or proxy, upgrade state, and logs.","Delete and recreate the Safe.","Change the target password manually."],"correct":0,"invest":["Open health and prerequisite results.","Correlate connector logs with the failed task.","Check service, DNS, proxy, certificate, and outbound path.","Check the connector-to-target protocol path.","Validate one task after recovery."],"avoid":"Declaring a full SaaS outage from one offline connector.","esc":"Connector health is normal but cloud tasks fail with a consistent correlation ID."}},"cas7":{"id":{"title":"Permission Safe Terlalu Luas","cat":"Governance","desc":"Operator yang seharusnya Connect-only ternyata dapat menampilkan password production.","evi":["Connect bekerja.","Show Password juga bekerja.","Policy internal melarang credential terlihat."],"hyp":"Retrieve Accounts permission atau inherited group membership terlalu luas.","choices":["Ambil permission matrix efektif dan bandingkan dengan RBAC yang approved.","Hapus seluruh membership Safe segera.","Matikan audit agar akses tidak tercatat."],"correct":0,"invest":["Capture member dan permission efektif.","Periksa direct serta group-based membership.","Bandingkan dengan desain RBAC.","Hapus hanya permission berlebih melalui approved change.","Pastikan Connect tetap bekerja dan Show Password ditolak."],"avoid":"Menghapus akses yang sah tanpa impact assessment.","esc":"Akses berasal dari nested AD group yang dimiliki identity team."},"en":{"title":"Overly Broad Safe Permission","cat":"Governance","desc":"An operator who should be Connect-only can display a production password.","evi":["Connect works.","Show Password also works.","Internal policy forbids revealing the credential."],"hyp":"Retrieve Accounts permission or inherited group membership is too broad.","choices":["Capture the effective permission matrix and compare it with approved RBAC.","Immediately remove every Safe member.","Disable audit so the access is not recorded."],"correct":0,"invest":["Capture members and effective permissions.","Check direct and group-based membership.","Compare with the RBAC design.","Remove only the excess permission through approved change.","Confirm Connect still works and Show Password is denied."],"avoid":"Removing valid access without an impact assessment.","esc":"The access comes from a nested AD group owned by the identity team."}}},"glossary":[{"term":"CPM","def":{"id":"Central Policy Manager. Windows service pembelakang layar yang memutar dan memverifikasi sandi. Menggunakan plugin/TPC untuk konek ke target.","en":"Central Policy Manager; performs credential verification, change, reconcile, and configured dependency updates."}},{"term":"PSM","def":{"id":"Privileged Session Manager. Server proxy/jump. Mengamankan endpoint asli target dengan merekam layar dan memblokir direct koneksi dari laptop user.","en":"Privileged Session Manager; proxies, isolates, monitors, and records privileged sessions."}},{"term":"PVWA","def":{"id":"Password Vault Web Access. Antarmuka UI (web). Tempat user request koneksi dan admin atur Platform/Safe.","en":"Password Vault Web Access; the web and API layer used for access, requests, account operations, and administration."}},{"term":"Safe","def":{"id":"Kontainer logis otorisasi. Menentukan SIAPA yang punya hak melihat, memakai, atau mengubah credential di dalamnya.","en":"A logical storage and authorization boundary that holds objects and defines member permissions."}},{"term":"Platform","def":{"id":"Kumpulan aturan (policy). Menentukan BAGAIMANA password di-generate (panjang, rotasi) dan tool apa yang dipakai PSM.","en":"A management policy describing how a class of accounts is verified, changed, reconciled, and connected."}},{"term":"Reconcile","def":{"id":"Operasi CPM. Saat sandi out-of-sync, CPM memakai Reconcile Account (akun admin ketiga) untuk mereset sandi managed account.","en":"A forced password reset using a separate privileged account when the managed password cannot be used."}},{"term":"Verify","def":{"id":"Operasi CPM. CPM login dengan sandi Vault ke target tanpa mengganti sandi, hanya untuk mengecek sinkronisasi.","en":"A test that confirms the credential stored in the Vault can authenticate to the target."}},{"term":"AppLocker","def":{"id":"Windows application control yang dapat memblokir executable connection component di PSM.","en":"Windows application control that can allow or block PSM connection-component executables."}},{"term":"CyberArk Error Code","def":{"id":"Kode error komponen membantu mempersempit layer, tetapi arti dan format harus divalidasi pada dokumentasi/knowledge base versi customer.","en":"A product error identifier that must be interpreted together with component, timestamp, version, and log context."}},{"term":"Use Accounts","def":{"id":"Permission di dalam Safe yang wajib dimiliki user agar tombol \"Connect\" muncul di PVWA.","en":"A Safe permission associated with using an account through an allowed connection flow."}},{"term":"Connector Management","def":{"id":"Interface/service untuk setup, health, prerequisite, lifecycle, upgrade, dan log connector di Privilege Cloud.","en":"The interface and services used to set up, monitor, upgrade, and troubleshoot Privilege Cloud connectors."}},{"term":"Digital Vault","def":{"id":"Repository hardened yang menjadi pusat object, credential, authorization, dan audit.","en":"The hardened repository at the center of CyberArk objects, credentials, authorization, and audit."}},{"term":"Managed Account","def":{"id":"Account target yang telah di-onboard dan ditangani lifecycle oleh CPM.","en":"A target account onboarded into CyberArk and governed by a Platform and Safe."}},{"term":"Reconcile Account","def":{"id":"Account lain dengan privilege reset yang digunakan saat managed account out-of-sync.","en":"A separate account with reset rights used to recover a managed account that is out of sync."}},{"term":"Logon Account","def":{"id":"Account perantara untuk login ke target atau masuk ke privileged mode.","en":"An intermediate account used to sign in before switching to a privileged context on certain target types."}},{"term":"Discovery","def":{"id":"Proses menemukan account privileged yang ada di environment sebelum dipilih untuk onboarding.","en":"The process of finding privileged accounts and related dependencies before onboarding decisions are made."}},{"term":"Account Feed","def":{"id":"Daftar hasil discovery/integrasi yang menunggu proses onboarding dan governance.","en":"A queue or view of discovered accounts awaiting review, onboarding, or governance action."}},{"term":"Credential Compliance","def":{"id":"Status apakah account mengikuti policy password, verification, dan change.","en":"The status indicating whether an account follows its verification, change, and policy requirements."}},{"term":"Access Window","def":{"id":"Rentang waktu saat request atau account access berlaku.","en":"The approved period during which a request or account access remains valid."}},{"term":"Exclusive Access","def":{"id":"Kontrol yang membatasi satu user agar memakai account pada satu waktu.","en":"A control that limits use of an account to one authorized user at a time."}},{"term":"Break-glass Account","def":{"id":"Account darurat dengan access sangat dibatasi, diaudit, dan biasanya dirotasi setelah dipakai.","en":"A tightly controlled emergency account whose use is audited and normally followed by rotation and review."}},{"term":"Service Account","def":{"id":"Account yang digunakan service, scheduled task, aplikasi, atau proses sistem.","en":"A non-human account used by a service, task, application, or system process."}},{"term":"Dependency","def":{"id":"Service, script, task, atau aplikasi lain yang menggunakan credential yang sama.","en":"A service, script, task, application, or connection that relies on the same credential."}},{"term":"Connection Component","def":{"id":"Konfigurasi executable/protocol/credential injection yang digunakan PSM untuk membuka session.","en":"PSM configuration that defines the client, dispatcher, protocol, and credential-injection behavior for a session."}},{"term":"NTP","def":{"id":"Network Time Protocol; sinkronisasi waktu penting untuk SAML assertion dan TLS.","en":"Network Time Protocol; reliable time synchronization is critical for SAML, TLS, logs, and incident timelines."}},{"term":"RTO/RPO","def":{"id":"Recovery Time Objective dan Recovery Point Objective untuk perencanaan DR.","en":"Recovery Time Objective and Recovery Point Objective; limits for acceptable outage duration and data loss."}},{"term":"Known Error","def":{"id":"Error pattern yang sudah punya diagnosis, workaround, atau approved fix.","en":"A repeatable failure pattern with a documented diagnosis, workaround, or approved fix."}},{"term":"Last Known Good","def":{"id":"Timestamp atau kondisi terakhir ketika flow masih berhasil; anchor penting untuk isolasi recent change.","en":"The latest time or state when the same flow was confirmed healthy, used to isolate recent changes."}},{"term":"Version-dependent","def":{"id":"Perilaku, menu, log path, atau prosedur yang harus divalidasi terhadap build environment.","en":"A detail such as menu, path, behavior, or procedure that must be checked against the actual product build."}}],"glossaryEn":{"CPM":"Central Policy Manager; performs credential verification, change, reconcile, and configured dependency updates.","PSM":"Privileged Session Manager; proxies, isolates, monitors, and records privileged sessions.","PVWA":"Password Vault Web Access; the web and API layer used for access, requests, account operations, and administration.","Safe":"A logical storage and authorization boundary that holds objects and defines member permissions.","Platform":"A management policy describing how a class of accounts is verified, changed, reconciled, and connected.","Reconcile":"A forced password reset using a separate privileged account when the managed password cannot be used.","Verify":"A test that confirms the credential stored in the Vault can authenticate to the target.","AppLocker":"Windows application control that can allow or block PSM connection-component executables.","CyberArk Error Code":"A product error identifier that must be interpreted together with component, timestamp, version, and log context.","Use Accounts":"A Safe permission associated with using an account through an allowed connection flow.","Connector Management":"The interface and services used to set up, monitor, upgrade, and troubleshoot Privilege Cloud connectors.","Digital Vault":"The hardened repository at the center of CyberArk objects, credentials, authorization, and audit.","Managed Account":"A target account onboarded into CyberArk and governed by a Platform and Safe.","Reconcile Account":"A separate account with reset rights used to recover a managed account that is out of sync.","Logon Account":"An intermediate account used to sign in before switching to a privileged context on certain target types.","Discovery":"The process of finding privileged accounts and related dependencies before onboarding decisions are made.","Account Feed":"A queue or view of discovered accounts awaiting review, onboarding, or governance action.","Credential Compliance":"The status indicating whether an account follows its verification, change, and policy requirements.","Access Window":"The approved period during which a request or account access remains valid.","Exclusive Access":"A control that limits use of an account to one authorized user at a time.","Break-glass Account":"A tightly controlled emergency account whose use is audited and normally followed by rotation and review.","Service Account":"A non-human account used by a service, task, application, or system process.","Dependency":"A service, script, task, application, or connection that relies on the same credential.","Connection Component":"PSM configuration that defines the client, dispatcher, protocol, and credential-injection behavior for a session.","NTP":"Network Time Protocol; reliable time synchronization is critical for SAML, TLS, logs, and incident timelines.","RTO/RPO":"Recovery Time Objective and Recovery Point Objective; limits for acceptable outage duration and data loss.","Known Error":"A repeatable failure pattern with a documented diagnosis, workaround, or approved fix.","Last Known Good":"The latest time or state when the same flow was confirmed healthy, used to isolate recent changes.","Version-dependent":"A detail such as menu, path, behavior, or procedure that must be checked against the actual product build."},"guides":[{"id":"g01","group":"Ticket Intake","title":{"id":"Sembilan pertanyaan awal L2","en":"Nine L2 intake questions"},"trigger":{"id":"Setiap ticket baru sebelum membuka log.","en":"Every new ticket before opening logs."},"steps":{"id":["Deployment: Self-Hosted atau Privilege Cloud?","Workflow: login, account visibility, Connect, session, Verify, Change, Reconcile, API, atau audit?","Scope: satu user/account/target/PSM atau semua?","Exact timestamp dan timezone?","Last known good dan recent change?","Exact error muncul di mana?","Apa yang sudah dicoba dan hasilnya?"],"en":["Deployment: Self-Hosted or Privilege Cloud?","Workflow: login, account visibility, Connect, session, Verify, Change, Reconcile, API, or audit?","Scope: one user/account/target/PSM or everyone?","Exact timestamp and timezone?","Last known good and recent change?","Where exactly does the error appear?","What was already tried and what happened?"]},"evidence":{"id":"Ticket intake minimum: impact, scope, version/build, topology, timestamp, user/account/target, error, recent change, attempts.","en":"Minimum intake: impact, scope, version/build, topology, timestamp, user/account/target, error, recent change, and attempts."},"avoid":{"id":"Menerima kalimat “CyberArk down” tanpa memecah workflow.","en":"Accepting “CyberArk is down” without decomposing the workflow."}},{"id":"g02","group":"Isolation","title":{"id":"Authentication vs Authorization vs Connectivity","en":"Authentication vs Authorization vs Connectivity"},"trigger":{"id":"User dapat login tetapi tidak melihat account, atau Connect gagal.","en":"User can sign in but cannot see accounts, or Connect fails."},"steps":{"id":["Authentication: apakah identity valid dan diterima IdP/directory?","Authorization: apakah user/group ada di Safe dan punya permission?","Connectivity: apakah host yang benar dapat mencapai destination/protocol?","Policy/application: apakah Platform, plugin, component, target policy, atau client yang menolak?"],"en":["Authentication: is the identity accepted by the IdP/directory?","Authorization: is the user/group in the Safe with the required permission?","Connectivity: can the correct source host reach the destination protocol?","Policy/application: is the Platform, plugin, component, target policy, or client rejecting it?"]},"evidence":{"id":"Jangan mengubah permission untuk menyelesaikan masalah network.","en":"Do not change permissions to solve a network problem."},"avoid":{"id":"Mencampur login, authorization, dan connectivity sebagai satu gejala.","en":"Treating login, authorization, and connectivity as one symptom."}},{"id":"g03","group":"PVWA","title":{"id":"PVWA dan authentication playbook","en":"PVWA and authentication playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"Portal unavailable, HTTP error, login loop, account kosong, Connect hilang, atau API gagal.","en":"Portal unavailable, HTTP error, login loop, empty account list, missing Connect, or API failure."},"steps":{"id":["Pisahkan browser/HTTP, IIS/app pool, authentication, Safe authorization, dan downstream component.","Untuk login loop: capture IdP event, PVWA log, time, certificate, claim, audience, dan redirect URL.","Login tetapi account kosong: periksa Safe membership dan List Accounts.","Account terlihat tetapi Connect hilang: periksa Use Accounts, Platform, connection component, approval, dan access window.","API saja gagal: periksa endpoint, TLS, token, permission, object ID, dan proxy."],"en":["Separate browser/HTTP, IIS/app pool, authentication, Safe authorization, and downstream component.","For a login loop: capture IdP event, PVWA log, time, certificate, claims, audience, and redirect URL.","Login works but accounts are empty: check Safe membership and List Accounts.","Account is visible but Connect is missing: check Use Accounts, Platform, connection component, approval, and access window.","Only the API fails: check endpoint, TLS, token, permission, object ID, and proxy."]},"evidence":{"id":"PVWA logs, IIS/Event Viewer, IdP event, HTTP status, exact URL, account/Safe scope.","en":"PVWA logs, IIS/Event Viewer, IdP event, HTTP status, exact URL, and account/Safe scope."},"avoid":{"id":"Restart semua komponen saat hanya satu authentication flow gagal.","en":"Restarting every component when one authentication flow fails."}},{"id":"g04","group":"CPM","title":{"id":"CPM Verify Failure playbook","en":"CPM Verify Failure playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"Verification Failed pada satu account, target, Platform, atau banyak account.","en":"Verification Failed on one account, target, Platform, or many accounts."},"steps":{"id":["Tentukan scope: satu account, target type, Platform, CPM, atau semua?","Uji reachability dan protocol dari CPM host ke target.","Periksa account disabled/expired/locked dan target-side security log.","Pastikan account, Platform, plugin, dan CPM assignment benar.","Cari apakah password pernah diganti langsung di target.","Bandingkan password policy dan authentication behavior dengan Platform.","Korelasikan CPM log dengan target response pada exact time."],"en":["Determine scope: one account, target type, Platform, CPM, or everything?","Test reachability and protocol from the CPM host to the target.","Check disabled/expired/locked state and target security logs.","Confirm account, Platform, plugin, and CPM assignment.","Check whether the password was changed directly on the target.","Compare target password policy and authentication behavior with the Platform.","Correlate CPM logs with target response at the exact time."]},"evidence":{"id":"Account ID, Platform, CPM, operation, exact error, target response, last known good, Verify history.","en":"Account ID, Platform, CPM, operation, exact error, target response, last known good, and Verify history."},"avoid":{"id":"Reconcile berulang pada service account tanpa impact analysis.","en":"Repeatedly reconciling a service account without impact analysis."}},{"id":"g05","group":"CPM","title":{"id":"CPM Change dan partial state","en":"CPM Change and partial state"},"trigger":{"id":"Password Change failed, target berubah tetapi Vault tidak pasti, atau aplikasi mati setelah rotasi.","en":"Password Change fails, the target changed but Vault state is uncertain, or an application dies after rotation."},"steps":{"id":["Tentukan titik gagal: old credential, target policy, target change, Vault commit, verification, atau dependency update.","Jika target changed tetapi Vault update tidak pasti, treat as high-risk partial state dan stop perubahan tambahan.","Periksa password policy: length, complexity, history, minimum age, forbidden characters.","Inventaris service, task, app pool, script, connection string, dan usage.","Uji recovery hanya melalui runbook/approval; jangan sync manual tanpa bukti."],"en":["Identify the failure point: old credential, target policy, target change, Vault commit, verification, or dependency update.","If the target changed but Vault state is uncertain, treat it as high-risk partial state and stop extra changes.","Check password policy: length, complexity, history, minimum age, forbidden characters.","Inventory services, tasks, app pools, scripts, connection strings, and usages.","Use only an approved recovery path; never manually sync without evidence."]},"evidence":{"id":"CPM job, target security log, account status, usage/dependency, application health.","en":"CPM job, target security log, account status, usage/dependency, and application health."},"avoid":{"id":"Membagikan password baru lewat chat.","en":"Sharing a new password over chat."}},{"id":"g06","group":"CPM","title":{"id":"Reconcile failure playbook","en":"Reconcile failure playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"Managed account out-of-sync dan Verify/Change tidak dapat memakai password lama.","en":"Managed account is out of sync and Verify/Change cannot use the old password."},"steps":{"id":["Konfirmasi Reconcile Account terhubung sesuai desain.","Validasi credential, target reachability, reset authority, dan target scope.","Periksa account lock, directory replication, policy special, dan target audit.","Tentukan dependency impact sebelum reset service account.","Setelah recovery, Verify dan application health wajib diuji."],"en":["Confirm the Reconcile Account is linked as designed.","Validate its credential, target reachability, reset authority, and target scope.","Check account lock, directory replication, special policy, and target audit.","Determine dependency impact before resetting a service account.","After recovery, verify the credential and application health."]},"evidence":{"id":"Reconcile association, CPM log, target reset evidence, dependency owner, approval.","en":"Reconcile association, CPM log, target reset evidence, dependency owner, and approval."},"avoid":{"id":"Mengubah password target dan Vault secara terpisah.","en":"Changing the target and Vault passwords separately."}},{"id":"g07","group":"PSM","title":{"id":"PSM/RDP session playbook","en":"PSM/RDP session playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"Connect tidak mulai, session disconnect, layar hitam, atau target menolak login.","en":"Connect does not start, the session disconnects, black screen, or target rejects login."},"steps":{"id":["Apakah user dapat login PVWA dan membuat request?","Failure sebelum PSM launch, saat Vault retrieval, atau saat PSM-to-target?","Scope user/target/PSM: satu atau semua?","Validasi DNS dan RDP dari PSM server yang sebenarnya.","Periksa PSM service, Windows events, component log, resource, dan recent change.","Pastikan Platform dan connection component benar.","Periksa AppLocker/hardening dan executable yang dibutuhkan.","Bandingkan dengan PSM/target yang sehat."],"en":["Can the user sign in to PVWA and create the request?","Does it fail before PSM launch, during Vault retrieval, or during PSM-to-target?","Is the scope one user/target/PSM or everyone?","Validate DNS and RDP from the actual PSM server.","Check PSM service, Windows events, component log, resources, and recent change.","Confirm the Platform and connection component.","Check AppLocker/hardening and required executables.","Compare with a healthy PSM/target."]},"evidence":{"id":"Session ID, PSM log, AppLocker event, target protocol log, DNS/port test, working comparison.","en":"Session ID, PSM log, AppLocker event, target protocol log, DNS/port test, and working comparison."},"avoid":{"id":"Men-disable hardening global.","en":"Disabling global hardening."}},{"id":"g08","group":"PSMP","title":{"id":"PSMP/SSH playbook","en":"PSMP/SSH playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"SSH session gagal, login berhasil tetapi command tidak jalan, host key/prompt berubah.","en":"SSH session fails, login works but commands fail, or host key/prompt changes."},"steps":{"id":["Validasi syntax, account, target, DNS, dan TCP path dari proxy.","Periksa SSH service, host-key behavior, authentication method, shell, dan prompt.","Pisahkan user authentication, Vault retrieval, target authentication, dan command restriction.","Bandingkan target gagal dengan target sehat pada Platform yang sama."],"en":["Validate syntax, account, target, DNS, and TCP path from the proxy.","Check SSH service, host-key behavior, authentication method, shell, and prompt.","Separate user authentication, Vault retrieval, target authentication, and command restrictions.","Compare the failing target with a healthy target on the same Platform."]},"evidence":{"id":"PSMP log, SSH server log, host-key event, target prompt, exact command behavior.","en":"PSMP log, SSH server log, host-key event, target prompt, and exact command behavior."},"avoid":{"id":"Menghapus host-key atau command restriction tanpa approval.","en":"Removing host keys or command restrictions without approval."}},{"id":"g09","group":"Identity","title":{"id":"SAML/SSO/MFA playbook","en":"SAML/SSO/MFA playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"Redirect loop, assertion ditolak, MFA error, atau hanya group tertentu gagal.","en":"Redirect loop, rejected assertion, MFA error, or only one group fails."},"steps":{"id":["Pastikan authentication method dan IdP yang benar.","Capture redirect sequence tanpa token sensitif.","Validasi NTP, certificate, entity/audience, reply URL, NameID, group claim, dan username mapping.","Tentukan scope one user, group, atau all users.","Bandingkan local/alternate auth hanya jika approved."],"en":["Confirm the authentication method and IdP.","Capture the redirect sequence without sensitive tokens.","Validate NTP, certificates, entity/audience, reply URL, NameID, group claims, and username mapping.","Determine one-user, group, or all-user scope.","Compare local/alternate authentication only when approved."]},"evidence":{"id":"IdP event, PVWA auth log, certificate expiry/thumbprint, time offset, claim mapping.","en":"IdP event, PVWA auth log, certificate expiry/thumbprint, time offset, and claim mapping."},"avoid":{"id":"Meminta user mengirim password atau token lengkap.","en":"Asking users to send passwords or full tokens."}},{"id":"g10","group":"TLS","title":{"id":"Certificate dan TLS playbook","en":"Certificate and TLS playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"TLS warning, API handshake gagal, integration trust error, atau renewal baru saja dilakukan.","en":"TLS warning, API handshake failure, integration trust error, or a recent renewal."},"steps":{"id":["Identifikasi path dan endpoint yang menyajikan certificate.","Periksa subject/SAN, issuer chain, expiry, trust, private key, dan binding.","Korelasi thumbprint, chain, format, service account, dan restart requirement dengan recent change.","Gunakan exact handshake error dan timestamp.","Siapkan rollback sebelum mengganti certificate production."],"en":["Identify the path and endpoint presenting the certificate.","Check subject/SAN, issuer chain, expiry, trust, private key, and binding.","Correlate thumbprint, chain, format, service account, and restart requirement with the recent change.","Use the exact handshake error and timestamp.","Prepare rollback before replacing a production certificate."]},"evidence":{"id":"Client/server certificate view, binding, chain, event log, handshake timestamp.","en":"Client/server certificate view, binding, chain, event log, and handshake timestamp."},"avoid":{"id":"Menganggap semua HTTPS error adalah certificate error.","en":"Treating every HTTPS error as a certificate error."}},{"id":"g11","group":"Cloud","title":{"id":"Privilege Cloud Connector playbook","en":"Privilege Cloud Connector playbook"},"trigger":{"id":"Portal cloud tersedia tetapi target internal tidak dapat diakses atau password task berhenti.","en":"Cloud portal is available but internal targets cannot be reached or password tasks stop."},"steps":{"id":["Periksa Connector Management health dan prerequisite.","Validasi service, outbound TLS/proxy, DNS, certificate, upgrade state, dan local log.","Korelasikan connector task/correlation ID dengan target protocol.","Pisahkan SaaS core, connector lokal, dan target internal.","Escalate dengan tenant, timestamp, connector identity, correlation ID, dan evidence lokal."],"en":["Check Connector Management health and prerequisites.","Validate service, outbound TLS/proxy, DNS, certificates, upgrade state, and local logs.","Correlate connector task/correlation ID with the target protocol.","Separate SaaS core, local connector, and internal target.","Escalate with tenant, timestamp, connector identity, correlation ID, and local evidence."]},"evidence":{"id":"Health result, connector log, service status, proxy/TLS evidence, target comparison.","en":"Health result, connector log, service status, proxy/TLS evidence, and target comparison."},"avoid":{"id":"Menghapus object Safe untuk memaksa recovery.","en":"Deleting Safe objects to force recovery."}},{"id":"g12","group":"Recovery","title":{"id":"Vault/DR safe boundary","en":"Vault/DR safe boundary"},"trigger":{"id":"Vault connectivity, replication lag, failover, corruption, atau recovery incident.","en":"Vault connectivity, replication lag, failover, corruption, or recovery incident."},"steps":{"id":["Collect health, topology, connectivity, replication status, logs, and recent change.","Tentukan apakah HA node failure atau DR/site/data event.","Ikuti customer-approved DR runbook dan escalation path.","Setelah recovery, validate login, account visibility, Verify/Change, session, audit, and monitoring."],"en":["Collect health, topology, connectivity, replication status, logs, and recent change.","Decide whether it is an HA node failure or a DR/site/data event.","Follow the customer-approved DR runbook and escalation path.","After recovery, validate login, account visibility, Verify/Change, sessions, audit, and monitoring."]},"evidence":{"id":"Replication status, Vault/component logs, RTO/RPO, failover timeline, validation results.","en":"Replication status, Vault/component logs, RTO/RPO, failover timeline, and validation results."},"avoid":{"id":"Melakukan failover atau repair Vault secara improvisasi.","en":"Improvising Vault failover or repair."}},{"id":"g13","group":"Implementation","title":{"id":"Onboarding account checklist","en":"Account onboarding checklist"},"trigger":{"id":"Account baru akan dimasukkan ke PAM atau pilot perlu acceptance.","en":"A new account is being onboarded or a pilot needs acceptance."},"steps":{"id":["Identify target, account, owner, purpose, criticality, and dependencies.","Validate CPM and PSM/PSMP reachability.","Select Safe, Platform, members, permissions, and connection component.","Onboard target address, username, current credential, Safe, and Platform.","Run Verify, controlled Change/Reconcile, authorized Connect, recording, audit, and handover."],"en":["Identify target, account, owner, purpose, criticality, and dependencies.","Validate CPM and PSM/PSMP reachability.","Select Safe, Platform, members, permissions, and connection component.","Onboard target address, username, current credential, Safe, and Platform.","Run Verify, controlled Change/Reconcile, authorized Connect, recording, audit, and handover."]},"evidence":{"id":"Discovery record, network matrix, Safe/Platform design, acceptance criteria, rollback, owner sign-off.","en":"Discovery record, network matrix, Safe/Platform design, acceptance criteria, rollback, and owner sign-off."},"avoid":{"id":"Onboard mass account tanpa pilot dan dependency inventory.","en":"Mass-onboarding without a pilot and dependency inventory."}},{"id":"g14","group":"Escalation","title":{"id":"Escalation package L3","en":"L3 escalation package"},"trigger":{"id":"L2 sudah mengisolasi issue tetapi membutuhkan product engineering, access, atau change authority.","en":"L2 has isolated the issue but needs product engineering, access, or change authority."},"steps":{"id":["Problem statement dan business impact.","Topology, deployment, version/build, user/account/target scope.","Exact timestamp/timezone, error, correlation/session ID.","Evidence relevan, steps tried, working comparison, and result.","Workaround/rollback jika approved.","Specific question untuk L3; bukan “please investigate”."],"en":["Problem statement and business impact.","Topology, deployment, version/build, and user/account/target scope.","Exact timestamp/timezone, error, correlation/session ID.","Relevant evidence, steps tried, working comparison, and result.","Approved workaround/rollback if any.","A specific question for L3—not “please investigate”."]},"evidence":{"id":"L3 harus dapat memahami issue tanpa bertanya ulang hal dasar.","en":"L3 should understand the issue without asking basic follow-up questions."},"avoid":{"id":"Dump semua log tanpa redaction atau password.","en":"Dumping every log without redaction or credentials."}}]};